{"parentUuid":"698a51a8-abfa-4f9e-b658-dd6d01826189","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"c02e84d4-fdda-494f-b43f-23d70efdff74","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nSaturday, October 03, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n\\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\\n\\n### Session (16:58)\\n\\n**Context:** Resumed a paused KeystoneOS / claude-skills audit session (AIOS Gate B/C work), then ran the `/mattpocock-skills:handoff` skill to capture state before stopping.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- The skill-roster checker was validated clean: 16/16 fixtures correct, agreement with the real YAML parser on all 42 skills, live roster failing only the 7 disabled skills, and all 4 fail-closed cases exiting 2.\\n- A sleep-induced API error plus a DNS failure (ENOTFOUND) cut off a response mid-run; the user said \\\"resume\\\".\\n- Claude could not invoke the handoff skill itself \\u2014 that skill is user-invocation-only, so the user had to type `/mattpocock-skills:handoff`.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Three independent items were approved and run: commit/push the checker fix in KeystoneOS, write the Gate B round 2 dispositions, and add Gate B round 2 to the execution log.\\n- Handoff doc written to the OS temp dir (not the workspace), linking to plan/log/report paths instead of copying content.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- Some plugin skills are gated to user invocation only; an agent cannot start them. Ask the user to type the slash command.\\n- Codex quota exhaustion (reset 10:41 PM) blocks review gates \\u2014 sequence Codex re-inspection around the reset rather than retrying.\\n- Staged-but-uncommitted fixes (C-01 executable bit) are easy to lose across a session break; commit before pausing.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Pending user decisions: (1) the 7 skills off in Claude but live in Codex/Pi \\u2014 ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, session-miner \\u2014 recommend retiring from canonical unless `library-review` or `pp-espn` is used in Codex; (2) Task 8 Pi trial step 1 needs `sudo` \\u2014 recommend the user runs it.\\n- Gate C remaining: commit C-01, fix C-02 (lock race), fix C-03 (usage counts cover Claude only).\\n- Codex re-inspection of manifest fix `7459560` after quota reset; then Gate D; then update `docs/STATUS.md`.\\n- Commit the BLOCKED Task 8 report at `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md`.\\n- Still-open task from earlier: write the project-level skill at `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` (8-part read-only audit procedure).\\n- Handoff file: `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-gate-c.md`\\n- Last commits: `7459560` (claude-skills), `08bf6e8` (KeystoneOS).\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":562},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4cd9b1be-a8db-4c78-8d09-19f38efd7126","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:10:16.814Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
{"parentUuid":"4cd9b1be-a8db-4c78-8d09-19f38efd7126","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"c02e84d4-fdda-494f-b43f-23d70efdff74","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \\\"timeline\\\")\\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\\n       - Each command: {label: \\\"section header\\\", command: \\\"shell command\\\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\\\"q1\\\", \\\"q2\\\", ...])\\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\\n\\n  <when_not_to_use>\\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\\n  </when_not_to_use>\\n\\n  <file_writing_policy>\\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\\n  </file_writing_policy>\\n\\n  <output_constraints>\\n    <artifact_policy>\\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\\n    </artifact_policy>\\n  </output_constraints>\\n  <session_continuity>\\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\\n  </session_continuity>\\n\\n  <ctx_commands>\\n    \\\"ctx stats\\\" | \\\"ctx-stats\\\" | \\\"/ctx-stats\\\" | context savings question\\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx doctor\\\" | \\\"ctx-doctor\\\" | \\\"/ctx-doctor\\\" | diagnose context-mode\\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx upgrade\\\" | \\\"ctx-upgrade\\\" | \\\"/ctx-upgrade\\\" | update context-mode\\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\\n\\n    \\\"ctx purge\\\" | \\\"ctx-purge\\\" | \\\"/ctx-purge\\\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\\n\\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \\\"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\\\"\\n  </ctx_commands>\\n\\n</context_window_protection>\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/sessionstart.mjs\"","durationMs":564},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c95e0edd-eda6-4631-88db-aed97efcc7db","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:10:16.817Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
{"parentUuid":"c95e0edd-eda6-4631-88db-aed97efcc7db","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\n# User Profile\n\n## About\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\n\n## Preferences\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\n\n## Working Style\n- Direct; says \"stop\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \"sharpened, not soothed.\"\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\n\n---\n\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\n\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\n# Working Memory\n\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\n\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\n- Prioritization slate LIVE 5/5 →Tier A prioritization-slate\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\n- FB matchups: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py` →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\n- Flint: NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify →`Flint`\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\n\n---\n\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\n\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)","## Today\nSaturday, October 03, 2026\n\n---\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here — read it only when a question actually needs it:\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`\n\n---\n\n## Recent Daily Log\n\n\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\n\n### Session (16:58)\n\n**Context:** Resumed a paused KeystoneOS / claude-skills audit session (AIOS Gate B/C work), then ran the `/mattpocock-skills:handoff` skill to capture state before stopping.\n\n**Key Exchanges:**\n- The skill-roster checker was validated clean: 16/16 fixtures correct, agreement with the real YAML parser on all 42 skills, live roster failing only the 7 disabled skills, and all 4 fail-closed cases exiting 2.\n- A sleep-induced API error plus a DNS failure (ENOTFOUND) cut off a response mid-run; the user said \"resume\".\n- Claude could not invoke the handoff skill itself — that skill is user-invocation-only, so the user had to type `/mattpocock-skills:handoff`.\n\n**Decisions Made:**\n- Three independent items were approved and run: commit/push the checker fix in KeystoneOS, write the Gate B round 2 dispositions, and add Gate B round 2 to the execution log.\n- Handoff doc written to the OS temp dir (not the workspace), linking to plan/log/report paths instead of copying content.\n\n**Lessons Learned:**\n- Some plugin skills are gated to user invocation only; an agent cannot start them. Ask the user to type the slash command.\n- Codex quota exhaustion (reset 10:41 PM) blocks review gates — sequence Codex re-inspection around the reset rather than retrying.\n- Staged-but-uncommitted fixes (C-01 executable bit) are easy to lose across a session break; commit before pausing.\n\n**Action Items:**\n- Pending user decisions: (1) the 7 skills off in Claude but live in Codex/Pi — ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, session-miner — recommend retiring from canonical unless `library-review` or `pp-espn` is used in Codex; (2) Task 8 Pi trial step 1 needs `sudo` — recommend the user runs it.\n- Gate C remaining: commit C-01, fix C-02 (lock race), fix C-03 (usage counts cover Claude only).\n- Codex re-inspection of manifest fix `7459560` after quota reset; then Gate D; then update `docs/STATUS.md`.\n- Commit the BLOCKED Task 8 report at `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md`.\n- Still-open task from earlier: write the project-level skill at `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` (8-part read-only audit procedure).\n- Handoff file: `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-gate-c.md`\n- Last commits: `7459560` (claude-skills), `08bf6e8` (KeystoneOS).\n","\n<context_window_protection>\n  <priority_instructions>\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\n  </priority_instructions>\n\n  <tool_selection_hierarchy>\n    0. MEMORY: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(sort: \"timeline\")\n       - On resume or compaction, query prior decisions, errors, plans, user prompts before asking the user — auto-captured session memory is searchable.\n    1. GATHER: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute(commands, queries)\n       - Primary research tool. Runs commands in parallel, auto-indexes each output, and (when queries are passed) returns matching sections in the same round trip — no follow-up search call.\n       - Each command: {label: \"section header\", command: \"shell command\"}; the label becomes the FTS5 chunk title — descriptive labels improve search.\n    2. FOLLOW-UP: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search(queries: [\"q1\", \"q2\", ...])\n       - Multiple related questions about anything already indexed (your captures + session memory). Batch every question in one array; the ranking pipeline runs per-query and the round-trip cost is paid once.\n    3. PROCESSING: mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute(language, code) | mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file(path, language, code)\n       - Derive answers FROM data: filter, count, aggregate, parse, transform. Only what you console.log() enters your conversation; the raw bytes stay in the sandbox.\n  </tool_selection_hierarchy>\n\n  <when_not_to_use>\n    - You intend to PROCESS the output (filter, count, parse, aggregate) → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute or mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute. Bash stays correct when you intend to OBSERVE a short fixed output (git status on a clean tree, whoami, pwd) or when you are mutating state (git, mkdir, rm, mv, navigation).\n    - You want to analyze, summarize, or extract from a file → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file. Read stays correct when you intend to Edit the file (Edit needs the exact bytes in your conversation to match against).\n    - WebFetch → use mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index; full network access, results indexed for mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search, raw page bytes never enter your conversation.\n    - mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute and mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file for file writes → these run code in a subprocess and discard the sandbox FS; they are for analysis, processing, and computation only.\n  </when_not_to_use>\n\n  <file_writing_policy>\n    File writes use the native Write or Edit tool — mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute, mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file, and Bash subprocesses do not persist edits to the host filesystem.\n    Applies to all file types: code, configs, plans, specs, YAML, JSON, markdown.\n  </file_writing_policy>\n\n  <output_constraints>\n    <artifact_policy>\n      Write artifacts (code, configs, PRDs) to files. Return only: file path + 1-line description.\n    </artifact_policy>\n  </output_constraints>\n  <session_continuity>\n    Skills, roles, and decisions captured earlier in this session are a memory aid, not a standing order. Treat them as context that may help — the user's most recent message always takes precedence. If a captured directive conflicts with what the user now asks, follow the user; a past phrase does not bind you.\n  </session_continuity>\n\n  <ctx_commands>\n    \"ctx stats\" | \"ctx-stats\" | \"/ctx-stats\" | context savings question\n    → Call stats MCP tool, display full output verbatim.\n\n    \"ctx doctor\" | \"ctx-doctor\" | \"/ctx-doctor\" | diagnose context-mode\n    → Call doctor MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx upgrade\" | \"ctx-upgrade\" | \"/ctx-upgrade\" | update context-mode\n    → Call upgrade MCP tool, run returned shell command, display as checklist.\n\n    \"ctx purge\" | \"ctx-purge\" | \"/ctx-purge\" | wipe/reset knowledge base\n    → Call purge MCP tool with confirm: true. Warn: irreversible.\n\n    After /clear or /compact: knowledge base preserved. Tell user: \"context-mode knowledge base preserved. Use `ctx purge` to start fresh.\"\n  </ctx_commands>\n\n</context_window_protection>"],"hookName":"SessionStart","toolUseID":"SessionStart","hookEvent":"SessionStart"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6225f0eb-b578-4813-806e-0e0e34e39994","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:10:16.819Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nSessionStart hook additional context: ## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\n\n<!-