{"parentUuid":"531fa31b-94e5-4564-9437-2576109bbfc1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- articulation-skill: Help users explain complex ideas simply to non-technical audiences with proven communication frameworks. Use when users need to explain technical concepts, structure presentations or writing, create clear documentation, improve communication clarity, or translate jargon into accessible language. Triggers include requests like \"help me explain this clearly\", \"how do I structure this presentation\", \"make this less technical\", \"help me articulate this idea\", or any request to simplify complex communication. Do not use for building a slide deck (use five-slides-generator or research-in-5) or for light copyediting of text that is already clear.\n- ArXiv\n- brain-audit\n- closeout\n- decision-audit: Decision Drain Audit: sort the decisions Eric has been avoiding into four buckets (decide now, needs one piece of information, waiting on someone, not mine), name why they are stuck, give 3 tiny next actions, then optionally decide them and record each answer where it lives. Use when the user says \"/decision-audit\", \"decision drain audit\", \"what decisions am I avoiding\", \"what's stuck\", \"fill out my pending decisions\", or \"let's work through the decisions\". Do not use for the Friday synthesis (use weekly-review), ranking projects (use project), or the biweekly report (use status-report).\n- interview-me\n- ISA\n- pp-catapult-openfield-connect\n- pp-zotero-research-library\n- research-in-5: Build a \"Research in 5\" weekly paper review for Baylor Athletics staff: a 5-slide deck (dark and light), a Teams post, and a staff email from one paper. Use when the user says \"/research-in-5\", \"research in 5 on this paper\", \"weekly research review\", \"review this paper for the staff\", \"make the slides for this paper\", hands over a paper (PDF, DOI, URL, Zotero item), or wants a review rebuilt or versioned (#001, v2). Do not use for a sport-science question (use sports-science-research-grounding), a deck with no single paper (use five-slides-generator), or a plain Zotero search.\n- Science\n- status-report: Build the every-two-weeks Applied Performance status report for Kenny Boyd and Chris Ruf — paste-ready email, one-page PDF, internal record. Use when the user says \"/status-report\", \"build my status report\", \"time for the Chris report\", \"biweekly update\", \"status update for Chris and Kenny\", \"what do I send Chris this week\", or when a scheduled report date arrives. Do not use for a single meeting brief (use meeting-prep) or the end-of-day supervisor log interview (use interview-me).","skillCount":12,"isInitial":false,"names":["articulation-skill","ArXiv","brain-audit","closeout","decision-audit","interview-me","ISA","pp-catapult-openfield-connect","pp-zotero-research-library","research-in-5","Science","status-report"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"91f1a96a-eac3-44b9-80ef-7f9a8995f97b","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:15:23.290Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- articulation-skill: Help users explain complex ideas simply to non-technical audiences with proven communication frameworks. Use when users need to explain technical concepts, structure presentations or writing, create clear documentation, improve communication clarity, or translate jargon into accessible language. Triggers include requests like \"help me explain this clearly\", \"how do I structure this presentation\", \"make this less technical\", \"help me articulate this idea\", or any request to simplify complex communication. Do not use for building a slide deck (use five-slides-generator or research-in-5) or for light copyediting of text that is already clear.\n- ArXiv\n- brain-audit\n- closeout\n- decision-audit: Decision Drain Audit: sort the decisions Eric has been avoiding into four buckets (decide now, needs one piece of information, waiting on someone, not mine), name why they are stuck, give 3 tiny next actions, then optionally decide them and record each answer where it lives. Use when the user says \"/decision-audit\", \"decision drain audit\", \"what decisions am I avoiding\", \"what's stuck\", \"fill out my pending decisions\", or \"let's work through the decisions\". Do not use for the Friday synthesis (use weekly-review), ranking projects (use project), or the biweekly report (use status-report).\n- interview-me\n- ISA\n- pp-catapult-openfield-connect\n- pp-zotero-research-library\n- research-in-5: Build a \"Research in 5\" weekly paper review for Baylor Athletics staff: a 5-slide deck (dark and light), a Teams post, and a staff email from one paper. Use when the user says \"/research-in-5\", \"research in 5 on this paper\", \"weekly research review\", \"review this paper for the staff\", \"make the slides for this paper\", hands over a paper (PDF, DOI, URL, Zotero item), or wants a review rebuilt or versioned (#001, v2). Do not use for a sport-science question (use sports-science-research-grounding), a deck with no single paper (use five-slides-generator), or a plain Zotero search.\n- Science\n- status-report: Build the every-two-weeks Applied Performance status report for Kenny Boyd and Chris Ruf — paste-ready email, one-page PDF, internal record. Use when the user says \"/status-report\", \"build my status report\", \"time for the Chris report\", \"biweekly update\", \"status update for Chris and Kenny\", \"what do I send Chris this week\", or when a scheduled report date arrives. Do not use for a single meeting brief (use meeting-prep) or the end-of-day supervisor log interview (use interview-me).\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"0949803b-b5a4-4eec-8bc8-87b3ccc4c359","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
