rame trees skipped; OneDrive-Import, team and athlete-facing folders, `00_INBOX` and all data files held (never sent out); Eric's own project docs routed by path.\n  - Jev input: 284 files. Jev answered all 284, 0 failures. Claude labelled them with the unchanged brief, and one review round gave GO AFTER FIXES (fixes applied).\n  - Result: tier A 101 (97 approved + 4 new). **Wave 2 approved by Eric and queued (`docs/QUEUE.md`):** Gabbett 2018, Gabbett and Oetter 2024, the Munich consensus, Boyle. Verify-first pair **verified 2026-10-03** (`docs/QUEUE.md`, below Wave 2): \"The System\" is the real Parker/Miller/Panariello book and is already W62; \"Black Book\" is Thibaudeau's *Black Book of Training Secrets*, queued 2026-10-03 as **X5** (Enhanced Edition, Eric's call).\n  - DONE 2026-10-01: Eric marked all 73 folders keep in `docs/onedrive-import-folders.md` (8,994 OneDrive-only files) and cleared all of them for Jev, Personnel, PERSONAL and HEALTH included. `HOLD_ROOTS` is now empty. **Run on Windows** (the catalog `data/triage.csv` and the TypeSafe path exist only there): `uv run scripts/triage_model_pass.py`, then `uv run scripts/jev_pass.py state`, then `uv run scripts/jev_pass.py run` (resumable; the 284 done keys are skipped). Then Claude labels the answers and Eric approves the shortlist.\n- **Next:** roots decided (2026-10-01, keep all, all to Jev); run the Jev pass on Windows (commands above); Claude labels; Eric approves the shortlist.\n- Still waiting on Eric from the 9/28 handoff: the Jev blind audit, the CLA primer questions, CVASPS listening.\n\n## Method interview (2026-09-28): DONE, answers applied\n- Eric answered all 27 interview-prep questions and the 6 peaking questions (merged to 30): `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`, in his words.\n- Its last section lists every change for `method-baseline.md` and the peaking synthesis. Biggest: course positions are Eric's (Explicit); Assessment Manual V12 and the V4 schedule are legacy; no true 