hortlists; the approved sources are Wave 1 in `docs/QUEUE.md`.\n\n## Day 3 (2026-09-28): gate done, promotion pending Eric\n- **Passed the gate, in staging only:**\n  - Issurin Ch4 (10 entries).\n  - Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2 (17 entries, new book).\n  - *Supertraining* 4.1 (6), 4.2a (15) and 4.2b (20).\n- **Review process:** each batch had an independent round-2 reviewer, not the fixer. Corrections were applied verbatim and are logged in `staging/fixes_*_applied.md`.\n- **Promotion dry run:** 69 new files. The only changed files are the two `_book.md`s. Unresolved links: 0.\n- **Ready to apply after promotion:**\n  - Reciprocal links: `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-28.md` (42 rows, 2 manual edits).\n  - `_domain.md` merge text: `staging/_domain_merge_sc_2026-09-28.md`.\n- **Vault:** unchanged. The last vault commit is still `aacbccd`.\n- **CVASPS transcript:** proposals are in `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md`. Its ASR check is not done: 47 flagged spots need listening before anything is cited.\n\n## Current state (2026-09-27, end of day 2)\n- **In the vault (SecondBrain `aacbccd`, pushed 2026-09-27):** 269 entries across 6 sources, all through the two-stage review gate, plus 66 reciprocal links. Staging was synced back from the vault (a promote dry run shows 0 changed).\n\n  | Book | Entries | Gate |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Harries *On-Field RTP* (`rehab-and-return-to-play/on-field-rtp--harries`) | 37 (33 + batch 2) | 2 rounds; batch 2: 1 round |\n  | Old Bull (`performance-technology-and-leadership/old-bull-performance-course--old-bull`), new domain | 37 | 2 rounds |\n  | Issurin *Block Periodization* Ch1-3 (`block-periodization--issurin`) | 28 | Ch1-2: 2 rounds; Ch3: 1 round |\n  | Bondarchuk *Transfer of Training* I, Ch1-2 (`transfer-of-training-in-sports--bondarchuk`) | 20 | 2 rounds |\n  | *Supertraining* Ch1-3 (`supertraining--verkhoshansky`) | 113 | Ch1: 3 rounds; Ch2-3a: 2; Ch3b: 1 |\n  | Landon Evans *Elite Sports Performance* (`elite-sports-performance--evans`) | 34 | 2 rounds |\n\n- **Search index:** memsearch re-indexed 2026-09-27; spot checks return the new Issurin, Evans, Old Bull and Supertraining Ch3 entries as top hits.\n- *Supertraining* is atomized through Chapter 3 (113 entries). Resume at Ch4 (printed 201, PDF idx 212).\n- CFTS OCR done 2026-09-27: `staging/ocr/cfts--francis.md` (218 pages, 0 low-confidence, 12 blank), so F3 in the queue is unblocked. Zatsiorsky 2e OCR (`bash scripts/ocr_zatsiorsky_2e_chunks.sh`, skips finished chunks) were rerun one at a time and both finished 2026-09-27 (CVASPS transcript: `staging/transcripts/landonevansphysicalpreparationinthencaaacomplementaryapproach.md`, unchecked draft).\n- All of this is on `main`: PR #1 merged 2026-09-27; the later `step1-triage` work (9/28-9/29) merged as PR #2 on 2026-10-01.\n\n- **OCR sources checked 2026-09-27.** Zatsiorsky 2e (`staging/ocr/science-practice-strength-2e--zatsiorsky--p*.md`, all 247 pages): the scan is missing about 2 printed pages in Ch10 (printed 205-214) and most of the Glossary and Suggested Readings (printed 227-238); Ch1-9 and Ch11 are complete (printed = PDF viewer page - 9 through PDF 213). Its OCR interleaves columns and sidebars, so read from page images. *CFTS* (`staging/ocr/cfts--francis.md`): all 11 chapters present in order; 12 blank pages are chapter-divider backs; no printed page numbers, so a missing page inside a chapter can only be caught by reading continuity; upside-down lines, dropped lines and figures are garbled despite \"0 low-confidence\". The OCR script (`scripts/ocr_pdf.py`) needs better column and rotation handling before the next scanned book.\n\n## Next\n0. 42 Analytics: 23 `supported` talks atomized to 152 staged entries (new domain `sports-analytics-and-decision-making`, book `ssac-talks--42analytics`); 50-entry Opus sample review done and fixes applied. **2026-10-02: second full round (r4a/r4b, 77 GO / 75 FIX / 0 NO-GO) then promoted on Eric's approval: SecondBrain `88acfc0`, 64 reciprocal links (`staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-02.md`), staging synced back. The r5 spot-check (20 entries, verdict fix-then-promote, 4 minor defects plus a 9-sentence sweep) ran after promotion and its fixes were applied in the vault. Codex full falsify review then checked all 152 current entries against the captions: GO AFTER FIXES, 53 PASS / 99 FIX / 0 NO-GO (`staging/review_42analytics_codex.md`). Main misses are 64 files with non-caption-exact quoted wording, 27 untagged `Eric's baseline:` lines, and 29 files with repeated numbers lacking a local locator. All 99 FIX rows then applied in the vault (two Opus fixers; several Codex locators were wrong and were corrected against the transcripts) and synced back: SecondBrain `ad006ad`. Post-fix checks: 0 untagged baseline lines, lint 0. Gate closed for this book. The two Jenkins causal-credit principles were then merged on Eric's call (SecondBrain `aa41109`): 151 entries.** Memsearch picks up the new notes on its next index run. See `docs/intake-42analytics.md`. The sources folder (`staging/sources/42analytics/`) is local only: recreate it on another machine from the `42Analytics` repo.\n0. **From 2026-09-29, most important first:**\n   - ~~(Eric) Mark keep or drop on `docs/onedrive-import-folders.md`.~~ Done 2026-10-01: all 73 keep.\n   - ~~(Eric) Open \"The System\" and \"Black Book Of Secrets\" (verify-first).~~ Verified 2026-10-03 (see `docs/QUEUE.md`). Black Book approved and queued as X5, Enhanced Edition (Eric, 2026-10-03).\n   - Ingest in queue order: the current queue, then Wave 1 (W1-W84), then Wave 2 (X1-X4).\n1. **Promotion is done.** For the next book (or a book already in the vault), repeat the recipe: `scripts/promote_to_vault.py` (dry run, then `--apply`), merge `_domain.md` by hand, `scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py`, commit and push SecondBrain, `memsearch index`, then `scripts/sync_back_from_vault.py` and commit in Flint.\n2. (Done: `step1-triage` merged into `main`, PR #1 on 2026-09-27 and PR #2 on 2026-10-01. Work on `main` or a fresh branch from now on; do not reuse `step1-triage`.)\n3. Add Eric's annotation to the vault Issurin 2016 brief: its \"concentrated unidirectional\" model is Verkhoshansky's, not Issurin's A-T-R (pp. 6-7, 11).\n4. Missing ideas logged by reviewers (in `staging/fixes_*_applied.md` and `staging/review_*.md`): a next atomizer batch per book. Biggest: Supertraining 3.3.3 strength and speed; Issurin's five Ch1-2 ideas; Harries speed prescription (kept inside broken-stride).\n5. Continue the queue (`docs/QUEUE.md`): *Supertraining* Ch4-9, Bondarchuk Vol I Ch3, then Zatsiorsky, Francis (CFTS once OCR is done), other Verkhoshansky books.\n6. CVASPS transcript: the draft exists, and the proposals are in `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md`. Next: listen to the 47 flagged ASR spots. After that, raise the 4 proposed Evans entries from `untested` to `supported` and atomize the new ideas.\n\n## Open questions\n- Interview (when Eric has time): `docs/interview-prep.md`, 27 questions. New: slide U4 L1 p.16 (Evans) has \"no more than 4x per year\" body-composition testing, which may be the origin of the same rule in `method-baseline.md`.\n- Evans Verkhoshansky activation-levels entry: the slides contradict themselves on where the threshold of adaptability sits; both are recorded and the entry stays `untested` (the course ceiling) rather than `contested`. Eric's call.\n- Two-a-day entry (Issurin): confirm the current NCAA Division I preseason practice rule before using it for fall camp.\n\n## Answered\n- **Mike Golden library priority** (open question): not the same priority as TB and Landon (Eric, 2026-09-29). Its tier-A files are in Wave 1.\n- **How to edit this worktree** (open question from 2026-09-26): enter the existing worktree by path (`EnterWorktree` with `.claude/worktrees/step1-triage`). The local sources (`staging/books`, `staging/ocr`, `staging/audio`, `staging/sources`) exist only there.\n\n## Gotchas\n- **After promotion the vault copy is canonical.** Reciprocal links and `_domain.md` merges are written in the vault only, so staging is synced back from it (Next 1.5). When re-promoting a book that is already in the vault (Supertraining after Ch4, Harries batch 3), any file the dry run reports as \"changed\" that you did not edit in staging means investigate, not copy: `--apply` would overwrite the vault version and drop its links.\n- **Fixer logs can overstate.** One Bondarchuk fixer log claimed fixes that were not in the files. Round-2 reviewers check the files, and fixers paste grep output. Run the lint (`python scripts/lint_library.py staging/library/<domain>/<book>` for body em dashes, review-history words, confidence and sections; `scripts/promote_to_vault.py` dry run for links) before promoting.\n- **Section headers** use the vault form `**What it is** —`. Agents drifted to `: mandatory` and `- mandatory` suffixes; normalized 2026-09-27.\n- **Reviewer \"(verify)\" citations** come from model memory. Never insert one unless the vault or the paper confirms it.\n- **Background jobs die with the session.** Run long OCR in `--pages` chunks to separate files (Zatsiorsky 2e is 247 pages, about 3 hours) so a death loses one chunk. CFTS: 218 pages, about 2.5 hours.\n- **Page numbers.** The ingest-book extractor's `--pages` is inclusive and has a `viewer_page` field (claude-skills PR #9). Entries cite the 0-based `page` (= `viewer_page` minus 1). The Mac needs `git pull` in `~/.claude/skills`, then the sync script.\n- **Codex runs on Eric's ChatGPT plan cap.** When capped, reviews use fresh Opus agents with `staging/review_book_prompt.md`.\n- **Every atomizer follows `docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md`**, which now carries the 2026-09-27 lessons.\n- **`staging/` tracking.** `library/`, `review_*.md`, `*_prompt.md`, `fixes_*.md`, `reciprocal_links_*.md` and `_scope_*.txt` are committed. Books, audio, sources and OCR stay local.\n- **`gws` output.** It prints \"Using keyring backend\" on stdout, and scripts filter that line out.\n- **TB attribution.** TB is shortcut-linked inside AP & Sports Science. The manifest skips shortcuts to other configured roots so TB keeps its own attribution.\n- **Triage patterns.** The rules match underscores as spaces, so folder-name patterns use `.` in place of `_`.\n- **After a catalog re-run** (or a roots.json priority change): `scripts/recanonicalize_manifest.py` if priorities changed, then `triage_rules.py`, `triage_model_pass.py`, `build_shortlists.py`, and confirm every labelled `candidate=yes` key is still tier A.\n- **Nothing record-shaped goes to Jev.** Held paths live in `HOLD_PATH` and `HOLD_ROOTS` in `triage_model_pass.py`; data files are always held. Judge from folder names; do not open a file to check.\nflint-handoff-2026-09-28.md\n2026-09-29-flint-shortlists-catalog-jev.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a936e81-c8c3-4bb6-8fdd-1fe11047a069","session_id":"0949803b-b5a4-4eec-8bc8-87b3ccc4c359","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
