t) | 221 | Targets the strength-and-conditioning miss-log gap from 2026-09-03 (\"peaking phase structure for collegiate football\"). Converges with Bompa's periodization entries and Bondarchuk's |\n| I2 | *Principles and Basics of Advanced Athletic Training* (Ultimate Athlete Concepts, 2008) | Landon library, same folder (clean text) | 242 | Training theory: adaptation, residual training effects, training loads |\n| I3 | Five peer-reviewed papers: \"Benefits and Limitations of Block Periodized Training Approaches\", \"New Horizons for the Methodology and Physiology of Training Periodization\", \"Training Transfer: Scientific Background and Insights\", \"Periodization Training from Ancient Precursors to Structured Block Models\", and the vibration strength study | TB snapshot, `SC Books/S&C Articles/Issurin, Vladimir/` | papers | Into **Zotero**, not `ingest-book`. The papers are where Issurin's claims meet peer review, so a book entry that a paper qualifies gets marked `contested` or linked to it |\n| I4 | Two Issurin presentations (Golden library) and the block periodization deck for rowers | Golden and Landon libraries | slides | Sparse slides (about 29 words a page). Cross-check only |\n\n### Charlie Francis, after Issurin (queued by Eric 2026-09-26)\n\n| Order | Source | Copy | Size | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | *Key Concepts, 2008 Elite Edition* (CharlieFrancis.com) | TB snapshot `Charlie Francis/Charlie Francis - Key Concepts Elite Edition.pdf` (text, about 400 words a page) | 270 pages | The best text source. Topics: speed, special endurance, tempo, high-low organization, CNS load |\n| F2 | Lecture videos, 13 files: *Team Sport Training Concepts*, *Peaking When It Counts: The 10-Day Taper*, *Vancouver Lecture 2004*, *Weights for Speed 1 to 3*, *Section 1: Adaptation and Training Element Selection*, *Practical Sessions 1 and 2*, *GPP Essentials*, *Passive and Active Recovery*, *Medicine Ball*, *Bike Workout* | `AP & Sports Science/Strength and Condi