{"parentUuid":"44b3031f-d022-42fa-8ca2-e5e2d19c27a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffTEN4S4jg8VkPWLk5Ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Picking up the next book step: *Supertraining* sections 4.3 and 4.4 (14 pages). I pulled the vault first, because the Mac copy was out of date. Now I am starting a writer agent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6003,"cache_read_input_tokens":120741,"output_tokens":2158,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6003,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":120741,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6003},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffTEMnKRpPQMDZBftizG","type":"assistant","uuid":"149fe16c-0980-4e2e-a1e1-3e7b8118f089","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:22:01.769Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"0949803b-b5a4-4eec-8bc8-87b3ccc4c359","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main","sessionKind":"bg"}
{"parentUuid":"149fe16c-0980-4e2e-a1e1-3e7b8118f089","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffTEN4S4jg8VkPWLk5Ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013YsLwPgne3PhZ4zGLrGdaR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Atomize Supertraining 4.3-4.4","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are a Flint ingest atomizer. Task: atomize *Supertraining* (Siff and Verkhoshansky, 6th Expanded Edition) Chapter 4 sections 4.3 \"Dynamic Correspondence as a Means of Strength\" (printed 241-247, PDF idx 252-258) and 4.4 \"Strength Training and General Endurance\" (printed 248-254, PDF idx 259-265) into library entries. Stop at the end of 4.4. Do NOT start Chapter 5.\n\n## Read first, in full\n1. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` — every rule is checked by a reviewer. Its paths are Windows paths; use the Mac translations below.\n2. `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/ingest-book/SKILL.md` — schema, frontmatter keys, file kinds.\n3. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md` — Eric's approved baseline (use as \"Eric's baseline:\").\n4. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md` — the map and resume checkpoint. Note the page key: PDF idx = printed + 11 (0-based index).\n5. Two existing entries in the same folder as a style reference (for example `claim--isometric-regional-specificity-not-strictly-angular.md` and one `principle--` file), plus `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch4-2b_applied.md` to see what reviewers flagged last batch.\n\n## Mac path translations (the brief has Windows paths)\n- Vault library (read-only, for dedup greps): `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`\n- Staging library: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`\n- Your output folder: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`\n- Source PDF (md5 d3453c5e459eb08ec0a89a4300a66e54, text layer with some OCR noise such as \"recognisc\"): `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`\n- Extract text with: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[252].get_text())\"`. For every figure or table you cite, render the page to PNG (`page.get_pixmap(dpi=150).save(...)` into `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/0949803b-b5a4-4eec-8bc8-87b3ccc4c359/scratchpad/`) and open it with the Read tool. Only write \"verified against the page image\" if you did that. Where OCR noise touches a number, check the page image.\n\n## Hard rules for this batch\n- Add NEW entry files only. Do NOT edit any existing entry file (the 4.1-4.2 and earlier entries are already in the vault). Dedup against vault and staging: earlier chapters already cover dynamic correspondence (grep \"dynamic correspondence\", \"specificity\", \"endurance\", \"concurrent\", \"interference\"). Add an entry only for a genuinely new angle and link the existing one in Related. List reciprocal-link suggestions in your report instead of editing other files.\n- In `_book.md`, the only edits allowed: set the 4.3 and 4.4 rows to `done` with entry counts (update after each section, not batched), and append a short batch-boundary note in the same style as the existing ones, saying resume at Chapter 5, printed 255 / PDF idx 266.\n- Use the source's own examples; otherwise start the Example with \"Inference:\". No mechanism the authors do not give. Record internal contradictions with both pages and set `contested`. Locators: \"PDF p. X / printed p. Y\" for every number, definition and quote. Write \"the authors\" unless a passage clearly belongs to one author.\n- No em dashes in titles or body text (the section headers `**What it is** —` keep theirs). No review history in entries. `created: 2026-10-03`.\n- Write a scope file `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch4-3-4.txt` listing your new entry filenames, one per line (same format as `_scope_supertraining_ch4-2b.txt`).\n- Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && python3 scripts/lint_library.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` (use `~/.local/bin/uv run` if python3 lacks deps) and fix what it flags in YOUR files. Paste the lint output in your report.\n- No git. No vault edits. Write only into your output folder and the scope file.\n\n## Final reply\nEntries by kind and by confidence; sections done with page ranges; reciprocal-link suggestions; unclear or contradictory spots in the source; anything you could not read; the lint output.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6003,"cache_read_input_tokens":120741,"output_tokens":2158,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6003,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":120741,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6003},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013YsLwPgne3PhZ4zGLrGdaR":{"description":"Atomize Supertraining 4.3-4.4","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"You are a Flint ingest atomizer. Task: atomize *Supertraining* (Siff and Verkhoshansky, 6th Expanded Edition) Chapter 4 sections 4.3 \"Dynamic Correspondence as a Means of Strength\" (printed 241-247, PDF idx 252-258) and 4.4 \"Strength Training and General Endurance\" (printed 248-