{"parentUuid":"b803ae6f-c7e6-4541-ba25-0a4881850e8c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:fork","toolUseID":"24758806-fd99-478a-af5d-cb7467747970","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\": {\"hookEventName\": \"SessionStart\", \"additionalContext\": \"## Today\\nSaturday, October 03, 2026\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Knowledge Base\\n\\n319 compiled articles (237 concepts, 81 connections, 0 qa). The index is NOT loaded here \\u2014 read it only when a question actually needs it:\\n- Full index (article, summary, sources, updated): `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/index.md`\\n- Article bodies: `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/<folder>/<name>.md`\\n- Search across all memory instead of reading the index: `memsearch search \\\"<query>\\\" --top-k 5`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recent Daily Log\\n\\n\\nFLUSH_OK - Nothing worth saving from this session\\n\\n### Session (16:58)\\n\\n**Context:** Resumed a paused KeystoneOS / claude-skills audit session (AIOS Gate B/C work), then ran the `/mattpocock-skills:handoff` skill to capture state before stopping.\\n\\n**Key Exchanges:**\\n- The skill-roster checker was validated clean: 16/16 fixtures correct, agreement with the real YAML parser on all 42 skills, live roster failing only the 7 disabled skills, and all 4 fail-closed cases exiting 2.\\n- A sleep-induced API error plus a DNS failure (ENOTFOUND) cut off a response mid-run; the user said \\\"resume\\\".\\n- Claude could not invoke the handoff skill itself \\u2014 that skill is user-invocation-only, so the user had to type `/mattpocock-skills:handoff`.\\n\\n**Decisions Made:**\\n- Three independent items were approved and run: commit/push the checker fix in KeystoneOS, write the Gate B round 2 dispositions, and add Gate B round 2 to the execution log.\\n- Handoff doc written to the OS temp dir (not the workspace), linking to plan/log/report paths instead of copying content.\\n\\n**Lessons Learned:**\\n- Some plugin skills are gated to user invocation only; an agent cannot start them. Ask the user to type the slash command.\\n- Codex quota exhaustion (reset 10:41 PM) blocks review gates \\u2014 sequence Codex re-inspection around the reset rather than retrying.\\n- Staged-but-uncommitted fixes (C-01 executable bit) are easy to lose across a session break; commit before pausing.\\n\\n**Action Items:**\\n- Pending user decisions: (1) the 7 skills off in Claude but live in Codex/Pi \\u2014 ArXiv, ISA, Science, capture-insight, library-review, pp-espn, session-miner \\u2014 recommend retiring from canonical unless `library-review` or `pp-espn` is used in Codex; (2) Task 8 Pi trial step 1 needs `sudo` \\u2014 recommend the user runs it.\\n- Gate C remaining: commit C-01, fix C-02 (lock race), fix C-03 (usage counts cover Claude only).\\n- Codex re-inspection of manifest fix `7459560` after quota reset; then Gate D; then update `docs/STATUS.md`.\\n- Commit the BLOCKED Task 8 report at `~/.claude/jobs/c59d1788/tmp/t8-pi-trial.md`.\\n- Still-open task from earlier: write the project-level skill at `~/DEV/KeystoneOS/.claude/skills/aios-audit/SKILL.md` (8-part read-only audit procedure).\\n- Handoff file: `/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/handoff-2026-09-13-aios-gate-c.md`\\n- Last commits: `7459560` (claude-skills), `08bf6e8` (KeystoneOS).\\n\"}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading knowledge base...","durationMs":240},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7dd49844-371e-4ffa-8bd2-2f66fae06437","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:26:20.936Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"7dd49844-371e-4ffa-8bd2-2f66fae06437","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:fork","toolUseID":"24758806-fd99-478a-af5d-cb7467747970","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n\\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\\n- Prioritization slate LIVE 5/5 →Tier A prioritization-slate\\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- FB matchups: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py` →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\\n- Flint: NEXT Eric: OneDrive keep/drop, 2 verify →`Flint`\\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n- **memsearch-sync** ×1 (2026-10-02 22:00 → 2026-10-02 22:00 UTC): index exit 1: grpc._channel._InactiveRpcError: <_InactiveRpcError of RPC that terminated with: (full output: C:\\\\Users\\\\eric_rash\\\\.claude\\\\global-memory\\\\transcripts\\\\.memsearch-index.log)\\n\\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4310 chars, updated 2026-10-02 11:26)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":242},"type":"attachment","uuid":"15f787f1-f19b-4f69-9ddb-08a8418bc3b6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:26:20.937Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"main"}
