{"parentUuid":"1011791b-1894-4c26-bf06-248b89183780","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3bfaadbd-f431-4350-8383-ef41e8ced49a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MGvNvRJGgD6Au1Fiwnj1H2","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Append reciprocal Related links from a staging/reciprocal_links_*.md table to vault files.\n\n    python scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md           # dry run\n    python scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-27.md --apply\n\nRun AFTER promote_to_vault.py --apply, so every source file is in the vault. Table rows:\n| source (path under Knowledge/library, domain optional) | [[target]] | location | text | origin |\nLibrary entries: the text is added as a new line at the end of the **Related** paragraph, or\na **Related** paragraph is created at the end of the file. Paper briefs: added as a bullet\nunder \"## Related knowledge\" (replacing a \"None identified\" placeholder). A row is skipped\nwhen the source already links the target.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nVAULT = Path(r\"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\SecondBrain\\Knowledge\\library\")\n\n\ndef resolve(src: str) -> Path | None:\n    src = src.strip().strip(\"`\")\n    hits = [p for p in VAULT.rglob(\"*.md\") if p.as_posix().endswith(\"/\" + src)]\n    return hits[0] if len(hits) == 1 else None\n\n\ndef add(text: str, line: str) -> str:\n    lines = text.rstrip(\"\\n\").split(\"\\n\")\n    if \"## Related knowledge\" in text:\n        i = next(k for k, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## Related knowledge\"))\n        j = i + 1\n        while j < len(lines) and not lines[j].startswith(\"## \"):\n            j += 1\n        block = [l for l in lines[i + 1:j] if l.strip() and \"None identified\" not in l]\n        if block and not block[-1].startswith(\"- \"):\n            block.append(\"\")\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines[:i + 1] + [\"\"] + block + [f\"- {line}\", \"\"] + lines[j:]).rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\"\n    rel = [k for k, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"**Related**\")]\n    if rel:\n        j = rel[-1] + 1\n# Reciprocal links from Flint's 2026-09-28 review wave\n\nCompiled from this wave's fix logs and round-2 reviews: `fixes_issurin_ch4_applied.md`,\n`review_issurin_ch4_opus.md`, `review_issurin_ch4_opus_round2.md`,\n`fixes_zatsiorsky_ch1-2_applied.md`, `review_zatsiorsky_ch1-2_opus_round2.md`,\n`fixes_supertraining_ch4-2a_applied.md`, `review_supertraining_ch4-2a_opus_round2.md`,\n`fixes_supertraining_ch4-2b_applied.md`, `review_supertraining_ch4-2b_opus_round2.md` and\n`fixes_supertraining_ch4-1_applied.md`. Every pair below was checked against the actual\ncurrent file content: source and target both confirmed to exist (in the vault library or in\none of the three staged folders promoted in this wave), each Source resolves to exactly one\nfile by `<book>/<file>.md` suffix once those folders are promoted, and the source file (vault\ncopy and, where one exists, staging copy) was scanned for an existing `[[...target-slug...]]`\nwikilink. Pairs already linked are listed under \"Dropped\" at the end, with the reason.\n\nPromoted in this wave: `strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`,\n`strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/` and\n`strength-and-conditioning/science-and-practice-of-strength-training--zatsiorsky/`. Every\ntarget below sits in one of these three folders and exists in staging today; none is in the\nvault yet. Run `apply_reciprocal_links.py` only after `promote_to_vault.py --apply` for all\nthree. Promotion overwrites vault copies with the staging copies, so the manual edits at the","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cbc47c2b-42aa-4513-ab2f-a08d24e9e7b1","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:32:48.079Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Append reciprocal Related links from a staging/reciprocal_links_*.md table to vault files.\n\n    python scripts/apply_recipr