{"parentUuid":"671d51b5-f087-4a2c-9299-9f1ee248db55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1fdfa3c5-04bc-4cbd-9261-b7deb5f4daa5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPEk5VydmGHLsXK3URfX5a","type":"tool_result","content":"fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/case-study--nfl-running-back-long-lever-wearable-resistance-sprint.md: body em dash lines [16, 26]\nfundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/claim--wearable-resistance-kinetic-energy-sprint.md: body em dash lines [14]\n+**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]]\n+**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]] (Supertraining 4.3.1: the authors call parachutes safer than weights added to the limbs or body because they add no vertical reaction force, but note that parachutes also resist the flight phase); [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]] (Supertraining 4.3.1, parachutes as another low-inertia resistance applied at sprint speed, with drag that rises with the square of running speed)\n+**Related** — [[claim--fiber-recruitment-not-simply-graded-by-force]]; [[claim--strength-training-raises-haemoglobin-myoglobin-and-aids-distance-sport]] (4.4, the other direction of interaction: the authors claim strength training raises haemoglobin and myoglobin and aids distance sport; rated contested)\n+**Related** — [[claim--energy-system-contribution-by-sport-table]]; [[block-periodization--issurin/case-study--warmup-cooldown-injury-reduction-soccer]]: Issurin's cool-down case now states the lactate/DOMS relationship in the same terminology-only terms this entry uses; [[claim--endurance-rests-on-muscle-oxidative-and-strength-qualities-not-vo2max]] (4.4, the authors' later muscle-centred view of lactate: stronger, more oxidative muscle makes less lactate and oxidises it in the muscle; rated contested)\n+**Related** — [[heuristic--strength-deficit-sets-training-method-choice]]; [[heuristic--rfd-as-correspondence-criterion-and-impulse-cannot-compare-movements]] (4.3.4, RFD used as a criterion of dynamic correspondence for choosing exercises when the time to apply force is short)\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e30dba3c-5125-4745-b165-cd2603cc1bbe","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:39:00.696Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"fundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/case-study--nfl-running-back-long-lever-wearable-resistance-sprint.md: body em dash lines [16, 26]\nfundamentals-of-sprinting--moyer/claim--wearable-resistance-kinetic-energy-sprint.md: body em dash lines [14]\n+**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/framework--five-criteria-of-dynamic-correspondence]]\n+**Related** — [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--parachute-resistance-tradeoffs-for-dynamic-correspondence]] (Supertraining 4.3.1: the authors call parachutes safer than weights added to the limbs or body because they add no vertical reaction force, but note that parachutes also resist the flight phase); [[supertraining--verkhoshansky/heuristic--parachute-resistance-sizing-progression-and-contrast-release]] (Supertraining 4.3.1, parachutes as another low-inertia resistance applied at sprint speed, with drag that rises with the square of running speed)\n+**Related** — [[claim--fiber-recruitment-not-simply-graded-by-force]]; [[claim--strength-training-raises-haemoglobin-myoglobin-and-aids-distance-sport]] (4.4, the other direction of interaction: the authors claim strength training raises haemoglobin and myoglobin and aids distance sport; rated contested)\n+**Related** — [[claim--energy-system-contribution-by-sport-table]]; [[block-periodization--issurin/case-study--warmup-cooldown-injury-reduction-soccer]]: Issurin's cool-down case now states the lactate/DOMS relationship in the same terminology-only terms this entry uses; [[claim--endurance-rests-on-muscle-oxidative-and-strength-qualities-not-