{"parentUuid":"a7389476-e5b5-41b0-acda-7c6bf9eea6db","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1fdfa3c5-04bc-4cbd-9261-b7deb5f4daa5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019GFVBieTNwaUEk4cx6exdA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# STATUS\n2\t\n3\t> **Latest handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-flint-shortlists-catalog-jev.md`** (DSI check, shortlists approved as Wave 1, wide catalog re-run and fixes, Jev pass, Wave 2 approved). Before it: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md`. All four staged batches now pass the gate: Issurin Ch4, Zatsiorsky Ch1-2, and *Supertraining* 4.1 plus 4.2. **Promoted to the vault 2026-09-28 (SecondBrain `ab3f042`, Eric's direct approval to the orchestrator):** 68 entries (Supertraining 4.1-4.2: 41; Issurin Ch4: 10; Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2: 17, new book) plus 42 reciprocal links and 2 manual edits; S&C `_domain.md` merged; staging synced back (0 drift); memsearch re-index started. Peaking synthesis rev 2 is waiting on Eric's six questions.\n4\t\n5\tRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n6\t\n7\t## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass\n8\t- **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts."}]},"uuid":"56c615b8-8ef8-4ac3-b016-0a180865f62d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:39:21.187Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# STATUS\n\n> **Latest handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-flint-shortlists-catalog-jev.md`** (DSI check, shortlists approved as Wave 1, wide catalog re-run and fixes, Jev pass, Wave 2 approved). Before it: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md`. All four staged batches now pass the gate: Issurin Ch4, Zatsiorsky Ch1-2, and *Supertraining* 4.1 plus 4.2. **Promoted to the vault 2026-09-28 (SecondBrain `ab3f042`, Eric's direct approval to the orchestrator):** 68 entries (Supertraining 4.1-4.2: 41; Issurin Ch4: 10; Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2: 17, new book) plus 42 reciprocal links and 2 manual edits; S&C `_domain.md` merged; staging synced back (0 drift); memsearch re-index started. Peaking synthesis rev 2 is waiting on Eric's six questions.\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass\n- **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts.","numLines":8,"startLine":1,"totalLines":107}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a7389476-e5b5-41b0-acda-7c6bf9eea6db","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"56c615b8-8ef8-4ac3-b016-0a180865f62d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ae6fb212-ca80-4913-8621-79f9c56f3636","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:39:21.213Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md:\n\n@AGENTS.md\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"ae6fb212-ca80-4913-8621-79f9c56f3636","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md","content":{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: Flint\n\n## What this is\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false,"parent":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/CLAUDE.md"},"displayPath":"AGENTS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba3113a1-99eb-4989-b8ba-d340ae6a044e","timestamp":"2026-10-03T15:39:21.213Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/AGENTS.md:\n\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: Flint\n\n## What this is\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\n\n## Conventions\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
