ult.py` and `lint_library.py` hard-code the Windows vault path. This session ran Mac-path copies from `staging/_tmp/` (gitignored); the repo scripts are unchanged. Fix: read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json`.\n- **Source oddities recorded in entries, not resolved:** Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV 2.7 (likely a misprint), the \"6% ... only 7%\" sentence (PDF 261), Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 is a treadmill study the book cites for strength training.\n- **Next for this book:** Chapter 5, The Methods of Special Strength Training, printed 255-312 / PDF idx 266-323 (58 pages, split into batches).\n","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":6,"newStart":4,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," Read this first. Update it before ending every session."," ","+## 2026-10-03 (Mac): *Supertraining* 4.3-4.4 promoted, Chapter 4 complete","+- **Source on the Mac:** the book is now staged at `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (copied from Drive `09_PRO_DEV/TB's Training Info (snapshot 2026-09-26)/Verkhoshansky/`, md5 `d3453c5e...` matches `_book.md`). Other staged books and OCR still exist only on Windows.","+- **Gate:** Opus atomizer wrote 23 entries (4.3: 13, 4.4: 10). Round 1 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus.md`): GO AFTER FIXES, 15 GO / 8 FIX / 0 NO-GO; worst miss was the power entry rating a wrong physics claim `proven`. Fixes applied and logged (`staging/fixes_supertraining_ch4-3-4_applied.md`); power entry renamed `claim--average-or-peak-force-times-velocity-is-not-power`. Round 2 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus_round2.md`): PROMOTE, 23 GO. Codex not used (independent fresh Opus reviewers).","+- **Promoted on Eric's approval:** SecondBrain `8d0909e` (23 entries + `_book.md`, Chapter 4 row now done, 64), then `104eb0e` (15 reciprocal links from `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03.md` plus 4 manual edits, incl. the Evans wrestling placeholder Related and stray `</content>` line). Staging synced back, dry run 0 drift. memsearch index of the library started 2026-10-03.","+- **Mac tooling gap:** `promote_to_vault.py`, `apply_reciprocal_links.py`, `sync_back_from_vault.py` and `lint_library.py` hard-code the Windows vault path. This session ran Mac-path copies from `staging/_tmp/` (gitignored); the repo scripts are unchanged. Fix: read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json`.","+- **Source oddities recorded in entries, not resolved:** Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV 2.7 (likely a misprint), the \"6% ... only 7%\" sentence (PDF 261), Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 is a treadmill study the book cites for strength training.","+- **Next for this book:** Chapter 5, The Methods of Special Strength Training, printed 255-312 / PDF idx 266-323 (58 pages, split into batches).","+"," ## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass"," - **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts."," - Peaking revision log now covers rev 3 (`docs/synthesis/_work/review_peaking_synthesis_opus.md`)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c7d968ed-481c-4a76-9a60-14236eacfd89","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
