ng library: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`\n- Output folder: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`\n- Source PDF (text layer with OCR noise such as \"D evelopm ent\"): `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`\n- Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. For every figure, table, equation or number near OCR noise, render the page (`d[N].get_pixmap(dpi=150).save('/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/5a_pN.png')`) and open it with Read. Only write \"verified against the page image\" if you did that.\n\n## Hard rules\n- Add NEW entry files only. Do NOT edit any existing entry and do NOT edit `_book.md` (the coordinator owns it). Dedup against vault and staging; much of this ground (maximum strength methods, speed-strength, strength deficit, autoregulation/DAPRE, velocity-based training) may be covered by Supertraining Ch1-4, Zatsiorsky, Issurin, Bompa, Moyer or the VBT guide. Add an entry only for a genuinely new angle and link the existing one in Related. List reciprocal-link suggestions in your report instead of editing other files.\n- Use the source's own examples, otherwise start the Example with \"Inference:\". No mechanism the authors do not give. Record internal contradictions with both pages and set `contested`. Locators \"PDF p. X / printed p. Y\" for every number, definition and quote. \"The authors\" unless a passage clearly belongs to one author (a passage naming Verkhoshansky in the third person is Siff writing).\n- Frontmatter `chapter:` uses the section number (e.g. \"5.2.2\"). `created: 2026-10-03`. No em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`). No review history. Never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines.\n- Write a scope file `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch5a.txt` listing your new filenames, one per line.\n- Lint: copy `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py` already exists with Mac paths: run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and fix anything flagged in YOUR files. Paste the output lines for your files.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\n## Final reply\nEntries by kind and confidence; entry count per section (5.1, 5.2, 5.2.1, 5.2.2, 5.2.3) with page ranges, for the coordinator's `_book.md`; reciprocal-link suggestions; unclear or contradictory spots in the source; anything you could not read; lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":191035,"output_tokens":6796,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":649},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6796,"cache_read_input_tokens":191035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CCBM77YmxEqh6YE3YG3UQe":{"description":"Atomize Supertraining 5a","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are a Flint ingest atomizer. Task: atomize *Supertraining* (Siff and Verkhoshansky, 6th Expanded Edition) Chapter 5, batch 5a: sections 5.1 \"The Problem of Methods\" through 5.2.3 \"The Development of Speed-Strength\", PDF idx 266-277 (printed 255-266). Stop where 5.2.4 begins (PDF 278). Two other atomizers are working at the same ti