tinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/f5b_pN.png` and open with Read for anything you touch.\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n- The 5 missing ideas: add an idea to an existing 5b entry where it fits; write a new entry only if no 5b entry can hold it, and then append it to the 5b scope file. Say which in the log.\n- Wilson citation: the reviewer's \"Wilson, Elliott & Wood, Med Sci Sports Exerc 1991\" is from model memory. Check it in Zotero (`mcp__zotero__search`) or PubMed (web search) before using it. If confirmed, record it in the prestretch entry as a source note with the reference; if not confirmed, leave the book's caption/text discrepancy as is and say so in the log.\n- If you rename any file, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths (a guard blocks shell variables), then grep all of `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library` for the old slug and update every staged inbound link.\n- Edit only the 5b files the review flags (plus any new entry). Do not touch `_book.md`, 5a or 5c files, or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice (\"Siff\" where the passage is his), locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history in entries, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: for each fixed file paste a grep showing the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky`. Paste both outputs in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), missing ideas placement, Wilson outcome, any renames, gr