ribution is wrong as a claim about when gains appear, but the error starts in Bompa &amp; Haff's book, not in the vault entry.\n- **What Bompa &amp; Haff write:** the 5th edition (PDF idx 61 in the Drive copy) says \"Siff and Verkhoshansky (83) suggested that performance gains may occur 4 to 12 weeks after the cessation of the concentrated loading phase.\" The vault entry repeats this faithfully, then turns it into a 4-12 week delay before performance lifts.\n- **What Supertraining says:**\n  - The wait before gains appear is 1-3 weeks (PDF 305).\n  - 4-12 weeks is how long the delayed training effect lasts (PDF 375). It starts when the block ends: Fig 6.31 shows gains rising right after the block.\n  - 4-12 weeks is also the length of the training stages themselves (PDF 305, 381, 536).\n- **Caveat:** I could not find Bompa &amp; Haff's reference 83 in the Drive copy.\n- **Suggested wording for the vault entry, for you to decide:** \"Bompa &amp; Haff cite Siff and Verkhoshansky for gains 4 to 12 weeks after the block; Supertraining itself gives a 1-3 week latency and 4-12 weeks as the duration of the delayed effect (PDF 305, 375).\"</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>311513</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>66</tool_uses><duration_ms>807652</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"b30603f9-747d-406f-9a86-892a0575492d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:22:13.266Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":4,"turnIndex":17},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
