ead off a graph.\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\". Note the review says \"p.288\" for the resistance-before-plyometrics rule; confirm its actual PDF index and printed page before citing it.\n- Fix 8 (allow restoration): record accurately that Bompa & Haff's book (not Supertraining) gives \"4 to 12 weeks after the cessation of the concentrated loading phase\", that Supertraining gives a 1-3 week latency (PDF 305) and 4-12 weeks as the duration of the delayed effect (PDF 375), and link the existing 4.1 delayed-gains entry (find its filename by grep). Do NOT edit the vault Bompa entry; describe it in the log under a heading \"Vault follow-up for Eric\".\n- If you rename any file, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths (a guard blocks shell variables), grep `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library` for the old slug, update 5c inbound links, and report any 5a/5b file that links the old slug (do not edit it).\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history in entries, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: for each fixed file paste a grep showing the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky`. Paste both outputs in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), the Fig 5.12 and 5.14 values you read, any renames, the vault follow-up text, grep proof, lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null