{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:25:43.090Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a943b4c4c92ae7c73</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01484ABtg4jJPCbtueu18jPL</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/a943b4c4c92ae7c73.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 5a round 2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** One fix is still needed, in one file. The other 18 entries can be promoted as they stand.\n\n**Counts:** 18 GO, 1 FIX, 0 NO-GO.\n\n**The one fix:** in `claim--implement-mass-for-speed-strength-keep-technique-and-size-per-athlete.md`, the When NOT section says \"only the shot and baseball data fit\" a stay-close-to-competition-mass rule. The baseball part is wrong. Round 1 suggested that wording and the fixer copied it in.\n- The page (PDF 276 / p.265) gives a 57 g light ball and a 184 g heavy ball against a regulation ball of about 148 g. The light ball is 61% under regulation, as far off as the counterexamples the same sentence lists. The heavy ball is 24% over.\n- That study measured precision transfer, not whether a closer mass works better.\n- Fix: say only the shot data fit. The exact replacement text is in the report.\n\n**What held up:**\n- **All 7 round-1 FIX entries:** every flagged problem is gone. Six are now GO; the implement-mass entry is the FIX above.\n- **Newton II physics:** correct line by line.\n  - The impulse of the net external force equals m(v_final - v_initial).\n  - The book's m.ΔV equals that only when the body starts from rest.\n  - Net propulsive impulse is measured from zero velocity at the bottom of the countermovement.\n  - The constant-gravity projectile example now correctly answers the book's sentence.\n  - `proven` covers only the identity.\n- **The fixer's five disagreements with round 1:** each is backed by the page.\n- **Links:** every wikilink in the 19 files resolves. The two old slugs appear nowhere in staging entries, scope files or the vault, only in the round-1 review and the fix log.\n- **Format:** all 19 files have the six headers once each, no em dashes outside headers, no wrapped links and no review-history wording.\n\n**GO entries spot-checked (6 of 11)**, against the page images:\n- `principle--speed-strength-strength-endurance-and-speed-endurance-are-independent-qualities`\n- `heuristic--analytical-synthetic-and-multifaceted-preparation-suit-only-early-training`\n- `framework--apre-autoregulating-progressive-resistance-exercise` (every cell of Table 5.2)\n- `case-study--arm-throw-height-after-barbell-press-tonic-work` (all 18 cells of Table 5.3, with the percentages recomputed)\n- `heuristic--cyclic-vs-acyclic-speed-strength-tempo-rest-and-fatigue`\n- `case-study--alternate-leg-bounding-with-thigh-cuffs-for-sprinters`\n\nI also re-checked the speed-strength loading entry, which the fixer edited; it is GO.\n\nThree small wording issues are listed in the report as optional; none blocks promotion. Pages 266, 273 and 275 were checked from the extracted text only, not the page images.\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5a_opus_round2.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>162291</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>35</tool_uses><duration_ms>313830</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
