{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:31:56.993Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3ff59f84f6364dea</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01PoVYZrPXuoJHeUDTUviXP9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/a3ff59f84f6364dea.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix Supertraining 5c entries\" finished</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>I applied all 11 fixes to the Ch5c entries, checking each one against the page first, and wrote the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md`. Every review claim held up on the page; I disagree only on some Fig 5.14 values. I did not touch any 5a/5b file, `_book.md` or the vault, and I renamed nothing, so no links changed.\n\nThe rule the review calls \"p.288\" is on PDF idx 288, and that page's printed footer reads 277. Entries cite it as \"PDF p. 288 / printed p. 277\".\n\n**Per-fix outcome**\n\n| # | Entry | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Deniskin | Applied, using my own Fig 5.14 readings (see disagreements below). |\n| 2 | Junior sprinters | Applied: new bar values, new comparisons against the sum of the two single groups, the unclear outlined bar flagged, Example updated. I also labelled the closing \"summation\" sentence \"Inference:\" and added the 30 m LS sum (0.25 vs 0.47). |\n| 3 | Novice sequencing | Applied. Removed the false mixed-sessions contradiction. Added the PDF 288 strand, the \"same day\" definition of mixed sessions, and the link. Added one sentence, labelled \"Inference:\", on why the two mixed-sessions statements do not conflict. |\n| 4 | Excess heavy strength | Applied (PDF 302 names both Filinov and \"excessive maximum strength training\"). |\n| 5 | Traditional circuit | Applied: the 10-15 reps at over 80% judgment is now labelled \"Inference:\" (PDF 313). |\n| 6 | Aerobic vs anaerobic circuits | Applied: the contested strand is narrowed, and the PDF 317 scheme is called a separate prescription. Still `contested`. |\n| 7 | Layout variants | Applied: the superset-planning sentence is labelled \"Inference:\". |\n| 8 | Allow restoration | Applied. The 4-12 week claim is placed on Bompa &amp; Haff 5e, not Supertraining. Supertraining gives a 1-3 week latency (PDF 305) and 4-12 weeks as how long the effect lasts (PDF 375). Added how Fig 6.31 shows the timing, read from the image. Linked `[[claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear]]`; the 18-25% after a 10-day rest is confirmed on PDF 213, and the entry is chapter 4.1.1. |\n| 9 | Sequence jumps-barbell-depth | Applied: dropped the mixed-sessions clause, set rule 1 (PDF 301) against PDF 299 and PDF 288, added the link. |\n| 10 | Accelerating specific adaptation | Applied: `contested` changed to `supported`, heading renamed. I also labelled the \"can coexist\" sentence \"Inference:\". |\n| 11 | Sequentially introduce means | Applied: the locator now points to PDF 308 / printed 297. |\n\n**Disagreements with the review** (small, recorded in the log):\n- **Fig 5.14 Ss values:** the review puts stage-3 Ss at about 700 falling to 650, highest at the start. I read it starting at about 665, peaking at about 685 in week 19 (mid-stage) and ending at about 625. The point stands: both curves fall within stage 3 and sit below their peak at the stage-4 test.\n- **Bompa &amp; Haff quote:** I could not open the book myself. It isn't in the staged books, and a search of the Drive folder had not returned when I finished. The quote and its PDF idx 61 locator come from the review, and the log says so.\n\n**Fig 5.12 (PDF 300), short / long / combined, in seconds:** I measured the short and long bar tops from pixels on a 300 dpi crop; the combined bars are read by eye.\n- 30 m LS: about 0.39 / 0.08 / 0.25\n- 30 m SS: about 0.08 / 0.14 / 0.19\n- 60 m LS: about 0.27 / 0.20 / 0.29\n- 60 m SS: about 0.07 / 0.38 / 0.42-0.43\n- 100 m LS: about 0.29 / 0.48 / 1.0\n- A white outlined bar at the right edge of the 100 m panel also reaches 1.0; it may be part of the frame, so it is marked unclear.\n\n**Fig 5.14 (PDF 301), Ss and Se:** the axis has numbers but no unit.\n- Ss: about 500 to about 565 across rest week 8, and about 610 to about 665 across rest week 16. It peaks at about 685 in week 19, falls to about 625 by week 21, and reads about 580-625 at the stage-4 test.\n- Se: about 280 to about 340 across week 8, and about 400 to about 430 across week 16. It falls to about 380 by week 21 and reads about 375-400 at the stage-4 test.\n\n**Vault follow-up for Eric** (I did not edit the vault): `periodization--bompa/principle--concentrated-loading-overreaching.md`, line 16, says \"Siff and Verkhoshansky note gains may appear **4 to 12 weeks** after the concentrated block ends; the longer/larger the loading, the longer the delay\". Line 22 says \"delayed-rebound timing (4–12 wk)\". The entry faithfully reports Bompa &amp; Haff 5e, but Supertraining 6e does not say this:\n- PDF 305 gives a latency of 1-3 weeks.\n- PDF 375 says the delayed effect lasts 4-12 weeks, about as long as the training stage.\n- PDF 381 and 536 use 4-12 weeks as the length of a stage.\n\n\"Longer loading, longer delay\" is in neither book. Suggested line 16: \"Bompa &amp; Haff cite Siff and Verkhoshansky for gains 4 to 12 weeks after the block; Supertraining itself gives a 1-3 week latency and 4-12 weeks as the duration of the delayed effect (PDF 305, 375).\" Line 22 would then read \"latency about 1-3 wk; effect lasting about as long as the block\".\n\n**Grep proof** (run from the book folder):\n```\nSs and Se jump after each rest week (weeks 8 and 16): Ss from about 500 ... Se from about 280 to about 340, and from about 400 to about 430\nBoth reach their highest values in stage 3 (Ss peaks at about 685 in week 19\nBoth then decline through stage 3 (Ss to about 625, Se to about 380 by week 21) and sit below that peak at the stage-4 test (Ss about 580-625, Se about 375-400) ...\n30 m LS about 0.39 / 0.08 / 0.25 s\nAn outlined bar at the right edge of the 100 m panel also reaches 1.0\nabove it only at 100 m LS (1.0 vs 0.77)\n(and at 30 m LS, 0.25 vs 0.47)\nabout 0.29 s for short jumps alone and about 0.48 s\nwith a rest interval between sessions on the same day\nprovided the resistance movements precede the plyometric activities in individual sessions\nInference: the first summary sentence\nthose two statements do not conflict\n[[claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers]]\ncovers both prolonged high volume (Deniskin) and excessive heaviness\nInference: 10-15 repetitions at over 80% of 1RM is beyond most lifters' capacity\nContested inside the book (muscle-endurance figures)\nis a separate prescription, not a contradiction\nInference: the superset equivalence is useful\nBompa &amp; Haff (5th ed.), not Supertraining\nFig 6.31 on that page (checked against the page image) shows the timing: ... T2, which begins where T1 ends (dashed line)\n[[claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear]]\nsits against the novice finding that this order\n[[claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers]]\nconfidence: supported\n**Two definitions in the book.**\nInference: the two can coexist\ncategorisation of the specific complex of means\" (PDF p. 308 / printed p. 297)\n--- old-phrase counts: 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0\n--- body em dashes / wrapped links in 5c scope: (end)\n```\n\n**Lint:**\n```\n$ ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 114, 115]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\nThe one issue is the usual false alarm on `_book.md`, which I did not edit. All wikilinks resolve, including the 3 I added.\n\nFor promotion: one confidence rating changed (accelerating specific adaptation, `contested` to `supported`). Two optional review items are left undone because their files are outside 5c: reciprocal links into the 5a depth-jump claim and the 4.1.1 delayed-gains claim. Page text and renders are in `staging/_tmp/f5c_fix_text.txt` and `staging/_renders/f5c_*.png`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>162607</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>43</tool_uses><duration_ms>569328</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
