rs/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r2_5c_pN.png` (use dpi=200 or higher for figures) and open with Read.\n\nScope of this round:\n1. Every file round 1 marked FIX (11), in full: each problem gone, each fixer disagreement justified by the page, nothing new wrong.\n2. Fig 5.12 (PDF 300) and Fig 5.14 (PDF 301): read the bars and curves yourself at high resolution and judge between the round-1 reading and the fixer's. Values read off a graph must say \"about\". Check every comparison the entries draw (sums of the single groups vs combined; rises and falls by stage).\n3. The allow-restoration entry: the 1-3 week latency (PDF 305), 4-12 weeks as duration of the delayed effect (PDF 375, Fig 6.31), stage length (PDF 381, 536). The Bompa & Haff quote was taken from round 1 and not seen by the fixer: if you can, find Bompa & Haff 5th ed on Drive (`/Users/kristinarash/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`, use `find ... -iname \"*bompa*\"` limited to a few minutes) and confirm the quote at PDF idx 61; if not found, require the entry to attribute the quote only as \"as Bompa & Haff are reported to state\" or similar and say so.\n4. Spot check at least 5 of the 15 round-1 GO entries against the page images.\n5. All wikilinks in the 26 files resolve (staging or vault). Every file: six section headers, no em dashes outside headers, no wrapped links, no review-history wording.\n\nWrite `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md`. Final reply: overall verdict (PROMOTE / GO AFTER FIXES with list / NO-GO), GO/FIX/NO-GO counts, which GO entries you spot-checked, and whether the Bompa quote was confirmed."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4244,"cache_read_input_tokens":251731,"output_tokens":1661,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":65},"server_tool_us