{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:37:32.754Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a88ee4dd63d94ec06</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NKxHwm5tCLi7Ww1NpKBBSd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/a88ee4dd63d94ec06.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 5c round 2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I wrote the round-2 report to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5c_opus_round2.md`. My verdict is **GO AFTER FIXES**.\n\n**Counts:** 25 GO, 1 FIX, 0 NO-GO. All 10 round-1 fixes besides the one below are in the files and correct. None of them introduced a new error.\n\n**Required fixes:**\n1. **Allow-restoration entry** (`heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next.md`):\n   - The Bompa &amp; Haff page is wrong. It should be PDF idx 60 / printed p. 49, not idx 61.\n   - \"That matches neither Supertraining statement\" is the writer's own judgment with no \"Inference:\" label. It is also only true one way: Bompa &amp; Haff's \"gains may occur 4 to 12 weeks after the cessation\" could mean a 4-12 week wait, or gains showing up during the 4-12 weeks after the block. The second reading is close to Supertraining's Chapter 6 figure.\n   - The entry should also quote Bompa &amp; Haff's own rule on the same page: the bigger and longer the loading phase, the longer before performance improves.\n   - The exact replacement text is in the report.\n2. **Fix log** (`fixes_supertraining_ch5c_applied.md`, \"Vault follow-up for Eric\"): it says the \"longer loading, longer delay\" rule is in neither book. That is false. Bompa &amp; Haff state it on idx 60 (refs 83, 91, 103, 104), so round 1's \"the vault entry sharpens it\" was wrong too. The vault Bompa entry reports its own book correctly on both points. The log's idx 61 page reference also needs correcting.\n\n**Fig 5.12 and Fig 5.14:** I measured both from 400 dpi crops.\n- **Fig 5.12:** my bar heights match the entry. All five sum comparisons hold: the combined group is below the sum of the two single groups at four distances and above it only at 100 m. The outlined area at the right edge of the 100 m panel really is ambiguous, so \"unclear\" is right.\n- **Fig 5.14:** the fixer's reading is right and round 1's was too high. Ss peaks at about 680 in the middle of stage 3, not about 700 at its start. Se is highest at about 430 at the start of stage 3. Every value in the entry says \"about\".\n\n**Bompa quote:** confirmed. It is verbatim in `~/DEV/BookInbox/Periodization - Theory and Methodology of Training - 5th.pdf`, which is byte-identical to the Drive copy, at idx 60 / printed p. 49.\n\n**GO entries spot-checked against page images:**\n- `framework--conditions-for-concentrated-unidirectional-loading` (PDF 305, 375)\n- `principle--converging-partial-effects-of-strength-training-means` (PDF 305-306, Fig 5.16)\n- `heuristic--replace-means-as-their-training-effect-fades` (PDF 308, Fig 5.18; Fig 5.19 on PDF 309 not re-opened)\n- `heuristic--setchinov-alternation-for-circuit-station-sequencing` (PDF 319, Figs 5.25-5.28)\n- `heuristic--circuit-progression-load-prescription-and-novice-pre-testing` (PDF 316-317)\n\nThe four-principles, specific-correspondence and early-specialisation entries also matched incidentally on the same pages.\n\n**Allow-restoration figures:** the 1-3 week latency (PDF 305), 4-12 weeks as how long the delayed effect lasts (PDF 375, Fig 6.31), and the stage lengths (PDF 381, 536) are all on the page as cited. One optional note: the Addendum on PDF 536 states the volume-versus-intensity warning in reverse of PDF 375, although its own triple-jumper example agrees with PDF 375.\n\n**Mechanical checks:** all 26 files have the six section headers, no em dashes outside them, no wrapped links and no review-history wording. All 174 wikilinks resolve in staging or the vault.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>176425</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>321467</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
