- 5c: (see the 5c writer list in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5c_opus.md` duplicates/missing sections and the 5c fix log). Include Issurin concentration-of-workloads -> conjugate sequence and concentrated-loading conditions; Issurin exercise-sequencing and concurrent-training case -> novice sequencing case and excess-heavy-strength claim; Issurin long-term four-stage and Bompa LTAD -> early specialisation; Bompa concentrated-loading-overreaching -> allow-restoration (CHECK: it was edited today and already links allow-restoration; if so, drop it as already linked); Bondarchuk sprint-strength transfer ceiling -> converging-partial-effects; Myszka donor-sport framework -> cross-training heuristic; research-papers Issurin 2016 brief -> conjugate sequence; plus Supertraining Ch1-4 sources the 5c writer named (continuous-vs-interval circuit claim, acute-delayed taxonomy, structured-load-progression heuristic, ES sequencing heuristic, four-level framework, functional-vs-nonfunctional machines, irradiation claim, parachute sizing, PAP framework).\\n  - Ch4.1.1 `claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear` -> allow-restoration (round-2 5c note).\\n  - The 5a depth-jump claim / 5b 475-jumps entry `claim--depth-jump-training-beat-higher-volume-traditional-training-in-jumpers` already links the 5c novice case? Check; if a new Ch5 entry should link another new Ch5 entry, those are in-batch and already reviewed; skip them unless the reviewers flagged them.\\n\\nFor every row: resolve both files by actual filename (use ls/grep; the short names above are descriptions, not slugs); confirm both exist in the vault; confirm the source resolves to exactly one file by `<book>/<file>.md` suffix; grep the source for an existing link to the target (if already linked, move to Dropped); read both files and write a one-line Related text that states the actual relationship accurately (no em dashes, plain style, `[[book/slug]]` cross-book, `[[slug]]` within the same book, match the source's link form). Sources must be OLD entries (not the 75 new ones). For text replacements (e.g. \\\"(see 5.x, not yet ingested)\\\" style placeholders in older Supertraining entries: grep the Supertraining folder for \\\"not yet ingested\\\" and \\\"Ch5\\\" / \\\"5.2.4\\\" / \\\"Chapter 5\\\" placeholders), put them under Manual edits with the exact current text and replacement, each confirmed to occur once. Drop suggestions the files do not support, with the reason. If a source has no **Related** paragraph or ends with stray content after it, note it.\\n\\nWrite `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03-ch5.md`. Final reply: script rows, manual edits, dropped (counts), the dry-run output line, and any doubts.\\n<context_window_protection>\\n  <priority_instructions>\\n    Every byte a tool returns enters your conversation memory and costs reasoning capacity for the rest of the session. The context-mode tools let you do the work in a sandbox and surface only the derived answer — the raw bytes stay out. Think-in-Code: program the analysis, do not compute it by reading raw data into your conversation.\\n  </priority_instructions>\\n\\n  <deferred_tool_bootstrap>\\n    The context-mode tools below may be DEFERRED in your harness — their schemas are not loaded yet, so calling them directly fails (e.g. \\\"tool not found\\\" / InputValidationError). Load them ONCE before your first ctx_* call:\\n    ToolSearch(query: \\\"select:mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_batch_execute,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_search,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_execute_file,mcp__plugin_context-mode_context-mode__ctx_fetch_and_index\\\")\\n    After that they are callable. If any ctx_* call fails as not-found, ToolSearch it and retry — do NOT fall back to Bash/Read just because the schema was not loaded yet.\\n  </deferred_tool_bootstrap>\\