i.org/10.1007/s40279-015-0425-5\r\n-\r\n-## Why it was promoted\r\n-\r\n-This review distinguishes concentrated-unidirectional and multi-targeted block models and provides a useful conceptual vocabulary for discussing concentrated workloads and sequencing.\r\n-\r\n-## Research question\r\n-\r\n-What benefits, limitations, and sport-context boundaries are reported for two versions of block-periodized athlete preparation?\r\n-\r\n-## Population and context\r\n-\r\n-- The review emphasizes elite, subelite, and well-trained athletes across endurance, team, combat, dual, jumping, and strength/power settings. [p. 11]\r\n-- It also discusses a smaller number of recreational-athlete studies.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ac79065f-ada7-412f-b80b-2bc6e39d5f2f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:15:28.000Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" M Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\n ...raining-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md | 153 +++++++++++----------\n 1 file changed, 77 insertions(+), 76 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md b/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\nindex f2f6408..22b6f9a 100644\n--- a/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\n+++ b/Knowledge/library/research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a.md\n@@ -1,76 +1,77 @@\n----\r\n-type: paper-brief\r\n-status: ingested\r\n-created: 2026-07-31\r\n-updated: 2026-07-31\r\n-source: zotero\r\n-zotero-item-key: PT9QTQ2I\r\n-zotero-attachment-key: 46JPR6ZS\r\n-zotero-version: 519