{"parentUuid":"6ab7733f-9aa0-4b6e-aaf7-d8b572d8ce4c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7ac19739-f7f3-4edb-be36-48155707b8e6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fir2bpXQgqtHykZJdv6ufM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# STATUS\n2\t\n3\t> **Latest handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-flint-shortlists-catalog-jev.md`** (DSI check, shortlists approved as Wave 1, wide catalog re-run and fixes, Jev pass, Wave 2 approved). Before it: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md`. All four staged batches now pass the gate: Issurin Ch4, Zatsiorsky Ch1-2, and *Supertraining* 4.1 plus 4.2. **Promoted to the vault 2026-09-28 (SecondBrain `ab3f042`, Eric's direct approval to the orchestrator):** 68 entries (Supertraining 4.1-4.2: 41; Issurin Ch4: 10; Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2: 17, new book) plus 42 reciprocal links and 2 manual edits; S&C `_domain.md` merged; staging synced back (0 drift); memsearch re-index started. Peaking synthesis rev 2 is waiting on Eric's six questions.\n4\t\n5\tRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n6\t\n7\t## 2026-10-03 (Mac): *Supertraining* 4.3-4.4 promoted, Chapter 4 complete\n8\t- **Source on the Mac:** the book is now staged at `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (copied from Drive `09_PRO_DEV/TB's Training Info (snapshot 2026-09-26)/Verkhoshansky/`, md5 `d3453c5e...` matches `_book.md`). Other staged books and OCR still exist only on Windows.\n9\t- **Gate:** Opus atomizer wrote 23 entries (4.3: 13, 4.4: 10). Round 1 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus.md`): GO AFTER FIXES, 15 GO / 8 FIX / 0 NO-GO; worst miss was the power entry rating a wrong physics claim `proven`. Fixes applied and logged (`staging/fixes_supertraining_ch4-3-4_applied.md`); power entry renamed `claim--average-or-peak-force-times-velocity-is-not-power`. Round 2 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus_round2.md`): PROMOTE, 23 GO. Codex not used (independent fresh Opus reviewers).\n10\t- **Promoted on Eric's approval:** SecondBrain `8d0909e` (23 entries + `_book.md`, Chapter 4 row now done, 64), then `104eb0e` (15 reciprocal links from `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03.md` plus 4 manual edits, incl. the Evans wrestling placeholder Related and stray `</content>` line). Staging synced back, dry run 0 drift. memsearch index of the library done 2026-10-03 (217 chunks, exit 0; new entries return as top hits).\n11\t- **Mac tooling gap:** `promote_to_vault.py`, `apply_reciprocal_links.py`, `sync_back_from_vault.py` and `lint_library.py` hard-code the Windows vault path. This session ran Mac-path copies from `staging/_tmp/` (gitignored); the repo scripts are unchanged. Fix: read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json`.\n12\t- **Source oddities recorded in entries, not resolved:** Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV 2.7 (likely a misprint), the \"6% ... only 7%\" sentence (PDF 261), Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 is a treadmill study the book cites for strength training.\n13\t- **Next for this book:** Chapter 5, The Methods of Special Strength Training, printed 255-312 / PDF idx 266-323 (58 pages, split into batches).\n14\t\n15\t## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass\n16\t- **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts."}]},"uuid":"459276c8-99f9-4fb6-9d80-6ec8ab2579cc","timestamp":"2026-10-03T17:15:45.725Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# STATUS\n\n> **Latest handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-29-flint-shortlists-catalog-jev.md`** (DSI check, shortlists approved as Wave 1, wide catalog re-run and fixes, Jev pass, Wave 2 approved). Before it: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md`. All four staged batches now pass the gate: Issurin Ch4, Zatsiorsky Ch1-2, and *Supertraining* 4.1 plus 4.2. **Promoted to the vault 2026-09-28 (SecondBrain `ab3f042`, Eric's direct approval to the orchestrator):** 68 entries (Supertraining 4.1-4.2: 41; Issurin Ch4: 10; Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2: 17, new book) plus 42 reciprocal links and 2 manual edits; S&C `_domain.md` merged; staging synced back (0 drift); memsearch re-index started. Peaking synthesis rev 2 is waiting on Eric's six questions.\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## 2026-10-03 (Mac): *Supertraining* 4.3-4.4 promoted, Chapter 4 complete\n- **Source on the Mac:** the book is now staged at `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (copied from Drive `09_PRO_DEV/TB's Training Info (snapshot 2026-09-26)/Verkhoshansky/`, md5 `d3453c5e...` matches `_book.md`). Other staged books and OCR still exist only on Windows.\n- **Gate:** Opus atomizer wrote 23 entries (4.3: 13, 4.4: 10). Round 1 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus.md`): GO AFTER FIXES, 15 GO / 8 FIX / 0 NO-GO; worst miss was the power entry rating a wrong physics claim `proven`. Fixes applied and logged (`staging/fixes_supertraining_ch4-3-4_applied.md`); power entry renamed `claim--average-or-peak-force-times-velocity-is-not-power`. Round 2 (`staging/review_supertraining_ch4-3-4_opus_round2.md`): PROMOTE, 23 GO. Codex not used (independent fresh Opus reviewers).\n- **Promoted on Eric's approval:** SecondBrain `8d0909e` (23 entries + `_book.md`, Chapter 4 row now done, 64), then `104eb0e` (15 reciprocal links from `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03.md` plus 4 manual edits, incl. the Evans wrestling placeholder Related and stray `</content>` line). Staging synced back, dry run 0 drift. memsearch index of the library done 2026-10-03 (217 chunks, exit 0; new entries return as top hits).\n- **Mac tooling gap:** `promote_to_vault.py`, `apply_reciprocal_links.py`, `sync_back_from_vault.py` and `lint_library.py` hard-code the Windows vault path. This session ran Mac-path copies from `staging/_tmp/` (gitignored); the repo scripts are unchanged. Fix: read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json`.\n- **Source oddities recorded in entries, not resolved:** Table 4.2 Class 1 factor IV 2.7 (likely a misprint), the \"6% ... only 7%\" sentence (PDF 261), Pattengale & Holloszy 1967 is a treadmill study the book cites for strength training.\n- **Next for this book:** Chapter 5, The Methods of Special Strength Training, printed 255-312 / PDF idx 266-323 (58 pages, split into batches).\n\n## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass\n- **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts.","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":115}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6ab7733f-9aa0-4b6e-aaf7-d8b572d8ce4c","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
