 book:** Chapter 5, The Methods of Special Strength Training, printed 255-312 / PDF idx 266-323 (58 pages, split into batches)."," ","+## 2026-10-03: Drive reorganized (project-triage org pass, step 8)","+- Files moved out of `00_INBOX` (which the regex skipped) and two career roots moved inside the primary drive (`11_PERSONAL/`, `10_ARCHIVE/`), so `exclude_path_regex` in `config/roots.json` gained `/11_PERSONAL/`, the career roots unanchored, `Device Backups & USBs`, `/Personnel/`, `WBB_athletes`, `Athlete_Performance_Overview`, `Spirit Squad`. Checked against the moved paths: all excluded; papers and decks still pass. Map of moves: `~/DEV/project-triage/docs/inventory/2026-10-03-drive-step8-plan.md`.","+- **Next for Eric:** re-run the catalog against the reorganized Drive (paths changed for ~100 items and 9 root folders).","+"," ## 2026-09-29: DSI check, shortlists, wide catalog, Jev pass"," - **DSI evidence check done:** `docs/synthesis/_work/dsi-evidence-check.md`. Measuring DSI is fine. As a plyo-vs-strength switch it is contested: IMTP PF explains 56-72% of DSI variance (Suchomel 2020), the 0.60/0.80 cutoffs were never validated and their attribution conflicts, and the one RCT (Pleša 2024, basketball, split at 0.90) found gains only in the strength arm. No American-football DSI data found. Baseline line updated, new Tension 17. Remaining hand-checks: SPORTDiscus, NSCA conference abstracts."," - Peaking revision log now covers rev 3 (`docs/synthesis/_work/review_peaking_synthesis_opus.md`)."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/config/roots.json","/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/STATUS.md"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"67a8d4dc-95a5-48c4-a401-f7f29e090d6b","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
