layed Training Effect\" and 6.11 \"The Dynamics of Training in the Annual Cycle\", PDF idx 363-378 (printed 352-367). Stop where 6.12 begins (PDF 379). Three other atomizers are working at the same time on 6.1-6.3 (PDF 324-346), 6.4-6.8 (PDF 347-362) and 6.12-6.17 (PDF 379-403); do not atomize their pages. If 6.8.3 starts on PDF 363 above the 6.9 heading, it is yours too; say so.\n\n## Read first, in full\n1. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (every rule is checked by a reviewer; Windows paths in it, use the Mac translations below).\n2. `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/ingest-book/SKILL.md` (schema, frontmatter keys, file kinds).\n3. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md` (Eric's approved baseline; quote lines verbatim with line number AND tag).\n4. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md` (map; page key PDF idx = printed + 11, 0-based).\n5. The Chapter 5 reviews, to avoid their errors: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch5a_opus.md`, `..._ch5b_opus.md`, `..._ch5c_opus.md` and their `_round2` versions. Common misses: unlabelled writer judgments, \"contested\" set for things that are not real contradictions, misread figure values, baseline quotes without tags, invented examples.\n6. Two existing entries in the output folder as style references.\n\n## Mac paths\n- Vault library (read-only, dedup greps): `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`\n- Staging library: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`\n- Output folder: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`\n- Source PDF (noisy text layer): `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`\n- Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render every page with a figure, table or number to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/6c_pN.png` (`d[N].get_pixmap(dpi=200).save(...)`) and open it with Read. Write \"about\" for values read off a graph. Only claim \"verified against the page image\" if you opened it.\n\n## Hard rules\n- Add NEW entry files only. Do NOT edit any existing entry and do NOT edit `_book.md`. Dedup against vault and staging. The long-term delayed training effect (LDTE) is ALREADY partly covered: Supertraining 5c `heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next` and `framework--conditions-for-concentrated-unidirectional-loading` cite PDF 375 and Fig 6.31; 4.1.1 `claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear`; Bompa `principle--concentrated-loading-overreaching` (just corrected: the 4-12 week claim is Bompa & Haff's citation; Supertraining gives 1-3 week latency at PDF 305 and 4-12 weeks as LDTE duration at PDF 375). Also Issurin residual effects, Bompa supercompensation, Zatsiorsky fitness-fatigue. Add an entry only for a genuinely new angle and link the existing one in Related; where another library source disagrees, record it and say which. List reciprocal-link suggestions in your report instead of editing other files.\n- Use the source's own examples, otherwise start the Example with \"Inference:\". No mechanism the authors do not give. `contested` only for a real contradiction or a named library source that disagrees; give both pages. Locators \"PDF p. X / printed p. Y\" on every number, definition and quote. \"The authors\" unless a passage clearly belongs to one author.\n- Frontmatter `chapter:` uses the section number. `created: 2026-10-03`. No em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`). No review history. Never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines.\n- Quality over coverage; stop at a clean section boundary if needed and say where.\n- Write a scope file `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6c.txt` listing your new filenames, one per line.\