{"parentUuid":"f50ae1d4-39ef-4f56-99e2-08df50e912ed","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffmuMZMkjHwKHK2Q67qs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part 6b is written: 16 entries, and the lint check is clean. Its first review is running now.\n\n**What 6b covers**\n- Sections 6.4 to 6.8.2: management, classifying sports, and how the body adapts to hard work.\n- **Management theory:** the writer skipped most of it, for example Maslow and the leadership grids, because the book does not apply it to training. It kept 3 models the book does apply to coaching, and each entry names whose model it is.\n- **A possible contradiction:** the book gives 3 different lengths for a hard training block: 3 to 4 weeks, 4 to 12 weeks, and \"up to 2 months\". The reviewer will check whether these measure the same thing.\n- **Your method notes:** the book says team sports run mostly on glycolytic energy (hard, short bursts). Your notes say football treats that work differently. The entry shows both views, each clearly labelled.\n\n| Part | Sections | Stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 6.1 to 6.3 | Writing |\n| 6b | 6.4 to 6.8 | First review running |\n| 6c | 6.9 to 6.11 | Writing |\n| 6d | 6.12 to 6.17 | Writing |\n\nYou do not need to do anything now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1768,"cache_read_input_tokens":325521,"output_tokens":416,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1768,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":416,"cache_read_input_tokens":325521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1768,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1768},"type":"message"}],"speed":"sta