{"parentUuid":"8ebf114f-6206-4d94-adcb-3df849926c35","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffn9wZtQ2SGaCkvHHmdC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Part 6a is written: 28 entries, and the lint check is clean. Its first review is running now.\n\n**What 6a covers**\n- Sections 6.1 to 6.3: how training plans grew over time, the types of periodisation (planning training in phases), how to set training loads, and the debate about periodisation.\n- **Voice:** section 6.3 talks about Verkhoshansky by name, so Siff wrote it. Verkhoshansky's views there are labelled as Siff's report of them.\n- **The writer found several places where the book does not add up.** Three examples:\n  - One table starts a training zone at 60%, but the text on the same page says 50 to 59%.\n  - The book says 75 kg gives the same 75% intensity, but 75 kg is only 62.5% of the 120 kg maximum.\n  - Two different figures are both numbered 6.2.\n- **Your method notes:** Verkhoshansky dismisses undulating loading, but your notes prefer it. The entry records this as a tension, with both views labelled.\n\n| Part | Sections | Stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 6.1 to 6.3 | First review running |\n| 6b | 6.4 to 6.8 | First review running |\n| 6c | 6.9 to 6.11 | Writing |\n| 6d | 6.12 to 6.17 | Writing |\n\nYou do not need to do anything now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1805,"cache_read_input_tokens":330712,"output_tokens":453,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1805,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":453,"cache_read_input_tokens":330712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tok