lume-and-contrast`:** PDF 371 calls order \"fairly unimportant\", then says to \"preserve the above order\". PDF 301 and 288 state fixed orders.\n- **Contested, `claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes`:** the vault brief of Issurin 2016 judges the evidence for Verkhoshansky's concentrated model insufficient for high-performance combat, team and swimming preparation.\n\n**Rows for `_book.md`:**\n\n| Section | Printed | PDF idx | Entries |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6.8.3 | 352 | 363 | 0 (covered by the two entries above) |\n| 6.9 lead-in + 6.9.1 | 352-355 | 363-366 | 3 |\n| 6.9.2 | 355 | 366 | 0 (Fig 6.27 is a contents/volume/organisation tree, no claim of its own) |\n| 6.9.3 | 356-358 | 367-369 | 2 |\n| 6.9.4 | 358-359 | 369-370 | 2 |\n| 6.9.5 | 359-362 | 370-373 | 5 |\n| 6.10 | 362-366 | 373-377 | 3 |\n| 6.11 | 366-368 | 377-379 | 4 |\n\nIn 6.9.3, the \"Specificity of the Load\" and \"Training Potential\" subsections were not re-atomized. The 4.3 dynamic-correspondence entries, `principle--training-effort-must-match-or-exceed-sport-effort-judged-by-movement-speed`, `heuristic--replace-means-as-their-training-effect-fades` and the other agent's 6.4 `framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions` already cover them.\n\nThe LDTE entries only add new angles and link the 5c entries rather than repeating them. The new material is:\n- the volume-optimum dose response;\n- \"not accompanied by marked signs of overtraining\";\n- points 1, 2 and 4, with the F1/F2/F3 reading;\n- the Fig 6.29 and 6.30 values;\n- the difference between maintenance and the LDTE;\n- the altitude-only evidence for endurance;\n- timing technique work to the LDTE window.\n\n**Unclear or contradictory spots in the source**\n- **Fig 6.24 (PDF 365):** the caption says \"% increase over initial values\", but the panel axes read kgf, kgf and cm. The caption's graph 2 and 3 descriptions also don't match the panel titles. I recorded the axis readings as \"about\" and flagged the units as unclear.\n- **Fig 6.24 vs Ch5 novice experiment 3 (PDF 299):** the design is almost identical, but Ch5 says novices and Ch6 says \"high jumpers of medium qualification\". The researcher names partly overlap. I recorded it as possibly the same study without asserting it.\n- **Text vs figure (PDF 369):** Fig 6.28 shows means A to D; the text names A, B and C.\n- **Text-layer error (PDF 364):** \"Chemousov\" is \"Chernousov\" on the page image.\n- **Cross-reference errors:**\n  - PDF 366 says \"(see 6.8)\" for what is actually in 6.10.\n  - PDF 364 prints \"the sum of the parts is greater than the whole\".\n  - PDF 371 points to \"Figure 1.7\", which is a torque diagram (PDF 28-29), so the intended scheme is unknown.\n- **PDF 370 wording:** anaerobic volume helps \"only if it precedes\" aerobic work. This reads against the aerobic-first order on PDF 373 and the negative pairing on PDF 372. I flagged it as unclear wording, not contested.\n- **Scope note, not a conflict (PDF 373 vs 369):** \"intensity rather than volume\" (Astrand &amp; Rodahl) sits beside 6.9.4's emphasis on volume. I read it as a scope difference.\n- **5.4.4 vs 6.9.5 on the first stage:** Fig 5.18 starts with low-intensity jumps, while PDF 372 starts with extensive submaximal resistance. I noted it as not a clean contradiction.\n\n**Pages read**\n- **As page images:** PDF 364-378 and 536, plus 300 dpi crops of Figs 6.24 and 6.25.\n- **Text layer only:**\n  - PDF 363 and 379. I didn't open the images for these; the entries say \"text layer\".\n  - The PDF 301 and 288 quotes. I checked them against the text layer, not the images.\n- **Nothing was unreadable.**\n\n**Reciprocal-link suggestions** (I edited none of these)\n- `framework--acute-delayed-particular-cumulative-training-effect-taxonomy` → `framework--temporal-and-qualitative-forms-of-the-training-effect`. Its \"6.7.1 not yet ingested\" note is now out of date.\n- These should link to `principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum`:\n  - `heuristic--allow-restoration-after-a-concentrated-block-before-the-next`\n  - `framework--conditions-for-concentrated-unidirectional-loading`\n  - `claim--delayed-strength-training-effect-lag-before-gains-appear`\n  - `claim--strength-detraining-and-retention-timelines`\n  - Bompa `principle--concentrated-loading-overreaching`\n- `case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments` → `case-study--barbell-and-depth-jump-sequences-in-high-jumpers`\n- `heuristic--sequence-jumps-then-barbell-then-depth-jumps-across-stages` → the within-session and sequential-accumulation heuristics\n- `claim--excess-heavy-strength-volume-impairs-speed-strength-and-technique` → the technique/LDTE heuristic\n- `framework--sequential-and-concurrent-variants-of-systematic-means` → `framework--three-viewpoints-on-organising-endurance-development`\n- `heuristic--structured-load-progression-beats-volume-alone-or-random-combination` → `principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue`\n- `claim--endurance-rests-on-muscle-oxidative-and-strength-qualities-not-vo2max` → `claim--middle-distance-runners-need-strength-and-jump-training-benchmarks`\n- The Issurin 2016 brief → the concentrated-vs-distributed claim\n- `framework--work-capacity-fitness-preparedness` → `framework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state`\n\nFive of my Related links point at files the other atomizers wrote this session. They resolve now but will break if those files are renamed:\n- `heuristic--keep-event-specific-competitive-stress-in-preparation`\n- `framework--logical-scheme-of-training-management-load-fitness-state-external-interactions`\n- `heuristic--concentrated-blocks-of-3-4-weeks-three-in-a-row-then-longer-recovery`\n- `principle--technical-mastery-needs-competition-intensity-practice`\n- `framework--supplementary-readiness-markers-hr-bp-ceff-palpation`\n\n**Lint output:** none of my 19 files is flagged. The only remaining issue in the folder is in `_book.md`, which isn't mine:\n```\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\n\nFiles are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`:\n- `principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum.md`\n- `principle--loading-volume-disturbs-homeostasis-and-prepares-connective-tissue.md`\n- `heuristic--time-technique-and-competition-strength-work-to-the-ldte-window.md`\n- `heuristic--within-session-order-of-explosive-means-matters-less-than-volume-and-contrast.md`\n- `heuristic--sequential-accumulation-needs-4-6-week-stages-extensive-before-explosive.md`\n- `heuristic--routine-artificial-restoration-can-blunt-adaptation.md`\n- `framework--positive-and-negative-sequences-of-endurance-loading.md`\n- `framework--three-viewpoints-on-organising-endurance-development.md`\n- `framework--three-levels-of-change-in-fitness-state.md`\n- `framework--temporal-and-qualitative-forms-of-the-training-effect.md`\n- `claim--ldte-in-endurance-training-documented-only-after-altitude-training.md`\n- `claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes.md`\n- `claim--time-limits-of-single-emphasis-loading-by-motor-quality.md`\n- `claim--annual-speed-strength-dynamics-depend-on-qualification.md`\n- `claim--middle-distance-runners-need-strength-and-jump-training-benchmarks.md`\n- `case-study--triple-jumper-plantarflexors-depressed-while-thigh-extensors-high.md`\n- `case-study--sirenko-double-peak-strength-means-for-middle-distance-runners.md`\n- `case-study--barbell-and-depth-jump-sequences-in-high-jumpers.md`\n- `case-study--nedobyvailov-light-heavy-and-combined-loads-in-jumpers.md`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>336361</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>92</tool_uses><duration_ms>1465642</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"746badde-515e-431d-a322-20250deab90a","ti