{"parentUuid":"fbcae2e6-6155-42bd-8e06-4e809a9387df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffni8xd9XBBM34bTNZqo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WtircdmtdbNW2r7DcEjvC5","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 6b entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX entries, 7 numbered fix groups, plus reciprocal-link suggestions and 5 missing ideas).\n- Standards: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (Windows paths; Mac vault is `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`, baseline `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md`).\n- Log format to copy: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`.\n\nFiles: the 16 entries in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6b.txt`, in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. Other fixers are editing 6a, 6c and 6d files in the same folder at the same time: edit ONLY 6b files.\n\nSource: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx (0-based) = printed + 11, covered PDF 347-362 (plus 305, 359, 375, 381). Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/f6b_pN.png` and open with Read for anything you touch. For Fig 6.22 render at dpi=400 and read graph A yourself before changing anything; the review says it is a decelerating curve consistent with the text's parabola, while the writer said it was nearly straight. Decide from the image; values off a graph say \"about\".\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n- Block durations: sort the numbers by what each measures, as the review lays out: concentrated block length (3-4 weeks PDF 360; 4-8 weeks PDF 305; \"up to 2 months\" PDF 381), single-emphasis stage length (4-12 weeks PDF 305 and 381), LDTE duration (4-12 weeks PDF 375), adaptation-reserve span (18-22 weeks). Keep `contested` only on the first group if those three truly conflict.\n- Distributed-vs-concentrated: name the critiqued model as Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model, compare the right quantities, and do not rule it out for medium-level athletes unless the page does.\n- Remove any process note mentioning other batches (\"batch 6a\" etc.) from entry bodies.\n- Missing ideas: the management-theory items (decision-making, management versus leadership, Blake-Mouton grid, needs theories) were skipped on purpose because the authors do not apply them to training on the page. Add one only if you find the authors DO apply it to training on the page; otherwise record \"not added: not applied to training\" in the log. The endurance monitoring point on PDF 359: fold it into an existing 6b entry if it fits.\n- Related links: add the review's suggested links only within 6b files and only to targets that exist today.\n- No renames unless required; if you rename, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths and report any 6a/6c/6d file that links the old slug (6c links several 6b files; do not edit them).\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history in entries, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines, baseline quotes carry line number and tag.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6b_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: grep each fixed file for the new wording, and grep 6b files for \"batch\" (expect none). Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and paste the lines for 6b files and the total. Paste both in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), the Fig 6.22 reading, any renames, grep proof, lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2157,"cache_read_input_tokens":349795,"output_tokens":1985,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":81},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1985,"cache_read_input_tokens":349795,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2157,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2157},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WtircdmtdbNW2r7DcEjvC5":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 6b entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX entries, 7 numbered fix groups, plus reciproc