{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:39:52.961Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5ff40d1cdbf45303</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015uMfAMS93nrJ7rq82n5H31</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/a5ff40d1cdbf45303.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix Supertraining 6a entries\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 6 fixes are applied and checked against the page images. I agreed with every one; none was wrong on the page. Log: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6a_applied.md`\n\n**The six fixes**\n1. **early-history:** applied. \"On the next page\" is now \"on the same page, directly after Dyson's five phases\". Confirmed on PDF 325.\n2. **progress-skills:** applied. \"Third bullet\" is now \"second bullet\", with the full bullet quoted and a locator to PDF 329.\n3. **volume-intensity calculation:** applied. The worked example keeps the 80 kg set (66.7% of 1RM), so it follows neither the 70% rule nor Chernyak's 40% rule (PDF 334). The percentage is my arithmetic, so it is labelled Inference.\n4. **cybernetic periodisation:** applied. The entry now says pages 339-340 name neither author and treats the method as the authors'. It also quotes 6.3's \"(see the section on Cybernetic Periodisation)\" on PDF 345, which goes slightly beyond the review's wording.\n5. **heart-rate tests:** applied. All 11 Table 6.5 ratios were recomputed from the image of PDF 341. The pulls at 0% now count as fitting the \"significant eccentric action\" qualifier, not as an inconsistency.\n6. **periodisation controversy:** applied. The British decline is now Verkhoshansky's own claim. Horwill and Tschiene are cited separately with their verbatim quotes (PDF 344).\n\nOne correction went beyond the review, in the controversy entry's Example. It said British \"middle-distance runners won Olympic gold before\" adopting the scheme. The page says \"middle distances\" of Soviet runners. For the British it says they \"did not gain gold medals ... over the last 30 years, but produced great achievements before\". The Example now quotes that sentence.\n\n**Optional items**\n- **Related links added to 6a files only, all targets confirmed to exist:**\n  - keep-event-specific gets the technical-mastery principle.\n  - training-cycle-hierarchy gets Evans's Bompa cycle types.\n  - backwards-plan gets the eight-step sequence, the mesocycle-boundaries entry and Evans's ten-step process.\n  - controversy gets the \"programming is an art\" principle.\n- **Missing ideas, all folded into the controversy entry:**\n  - The five-year-plan argument and Zheljazkov's partial agreement are quoted (PDF 345).\n  - Tschiene is covered by fix 6.\n  - Chronobiology (PDF 346-347) is a new paragraph marked \"Confidence for this part: `untested`\". It says the text gives no study linking circadian clocks to training cycles.\n- **Not done:** the optional Fig 6.7 axis note on the intensity-zone entry, because your instructions limited optional work to links and missing ideas. It is listed in the log for you.\n\nThere are no new entries and no renames, and the scope file is unchanged at 28 lines. I touched no 6b, 6c or 6d file, `_book.md` or the vault. Four links back from 6b-6d files are listed in the log for you to add.\n\n**Grep proof** (from the book folder)\n```\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:20:(Verkhoshansky's own claim)\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:20:He cites Horwill (1992, 1995)\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:20:has not changed from the moment of Matveyev's first formalisation\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:20:five year plans\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:22:partly agrees\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:24:Chronobiology, the section's closing argument\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:24:Confidence for this part: `untested`\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:32:did not gain gold medals on Olympic games\nclaim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md:34:programming-is-an-art-on-principles-not-an-algorithm\nframework--cybernetic-periodisation-rpe-and-rating-of-technique.md:24:pages 339-340 do not attribute the method to either author\nframework--cybernetic-periodisation-rpe-and-rating-of-technique.md:24:treat it as the authors'\nframework--early-history-of-periodisation-kotov-to-dyson.md:30:warn on the same page, directly after Dyson's five phases\nframework--training-cycle-hierarchy-durations-and-russian-term-swap.md:34:bompa-annual-plan-cycle-types\nframework--volume-intensity-and-relative-intensity-calculation.md:30:keeps the 80 kg set, which is 66.7% of the 120 kg 1RM\nframework--volume-intensity-and-relative-intensity-calculation.md:30:follows neither the 70% warm-up rule\nheuristic--keep-event-specific-competitive-stress-in-preparation.md:26:technical-mastery-needs-competition-intensity-practice\nheuristic--build-the-annual-plan-backwards-from-competitions.md:32:eight-step-sequence-for-programming-annual-training\nheuristic--build-the-annual-plan-backwards-from-competitions.md:32:set-mesocycle-boundaries-by-main-competition-dates\nheuristic--build-the-annual-plan-backwards-from-competitions.md:32:ten-step-process-for-building-an-annual-plan\nheuristic--heart-rate-work-capacity-tests-for-lifters.md:24:bench press +100% and squat clean about +88% exceed it\nheuristic--heart-rate-work-capacity-tests-for-lifters.md:24:the clean and snatch pulls at 0% fit the \"significant eccentric action\" qualifier\nheuristic--progress-skills-only-at-70-80-percent-technical-reliability.md:22:the second bullet in the source list\n```\nNone of the 28 files still contains any of the old phrases. Across all of them, the checks found no em dashes outside section headers, no wikilinks wrapped across lines and no review-history wording.\n\n**Lint**\n```\n$ ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\nNo 6a file has a lint line. The one issue is the known `_book.md` false positive, which is outside this task.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>151454</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>224912</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
