{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T18:44:49.351Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aff5f77e5ff2eecdd</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01DNgMaqhbrYHzn5PZrGDQ7n</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/aff5f77e5ff2eecdd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 6a round 2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** The batch needs one fix, a single sentence in the controversy entry. Counts: **GO 27, FIX 1, NO-GO 0.** All six round-1 fixes landed correctly. The fix log's claims all match the files and none are overstated.\n\n**The one fix**, in `claim--periodisation-controversy-verkhoshansky-vs-zheljazkov.md`, chronobiology paragraph: the sentence \"This is the section's only physiological argument for cycled training.\" is an unlabelled judgment. The book never says it, and it echoes round 1's wording. It is also arguable, because Zheljazkov makes a physiological point on PDF 345-346. Replace it with:\n\n&gt; Inference: this is the only passage in 6.3 that offers a biological mechanism in support of cycled training; Zheljazkov's physiological point (heterochronous restoration, PDF p. 345-346) argues for modifying periodisation, not for cycling as such.\n\nA grep is enough to confirm it; no third review round is needed.\n\n**The controversy entry, apart from that sentence:**\n- **Quotes:** every quoted string (about 40) is verbatim on PDF 344-347. I matched them against the page text, and checked the words the text layer garbles on the page images.\n- **Voices:** they are right.\n  - The Horwill and Tschiene citations are both Verkhoshansky's (\"refers to articles by Horwill\", \"Verkhoshansky cites the work of Tschiene\", PDF 344). The British-decline claim is also his.\n  - The five-year-plan argument is Verkhoshansky's as reported by Siff (\"He makes the interesting observation\", PDF 345).\n  - Zheljazkov's partial agreement is verbatim; the \"...\" drops only the word \"that\".\n- **Example:** the corrected Example quotes PDF 344-345 exactly.\n- **Chronobiology confidence:** the `untested` label is explicit, and the entry's overall `contested` is unchanged and still explained, so nothing shifted silently.\n\n**Heart-rate entry, Table 6.5:** all 11 rows match the PDF 341 image. I recomputed all nine non-zero ratios, not just four: +71, +68, +100, +88, +40, +6, +49, +11, +33%. Every percentage in the entry is right, and the \"significant eccentric action\" qualifier is verbatim.\n\n**GO entries spot-checked (6):**\n- **`claim--vorobyev-mean-training-weight-by-bodymass-and-qualification`:** 20 cells of Table 6.2 match the PDF 336 image.\n- **`framework--intensity-zone-distribution-and-load-recording`:** Table 6.1 headers and Fig 6.7 match the PDF 335 image. Round 1's optional note on the Fig 6.7 axis label (\"50+\") is still not applied; it was optional.\n- **`claim--chernyak-volume-intensity-week-combinations`:** all week counts and both same-page contradictions match PDF 343.\n- **`case-study--vorobyev-ermakov-weightlifting-load-distributions`:** Figs 6.2 to 6.5 match PDF 333.\n- **`heuristic--rule-of-sixty-percent-light-day-volume`:** quote checked on the PDF 329 text, plus the Fig 6.3A image.\n- **`framework--supplementary-readiness-markers-hr-bp-ceff-palpation`:** the heart-rate modes and blood-pressure passage match the PDF 341 image. I did not recheck its PDF 342 part (Ceff and palpation).\n\n**Checks on all 28 files:** every file has the six section headers once each, with no em dashes outside the headers, no wrapped links and no review-history wording. All 165 wikilinks resolve, including the ones added in the fix round.\n\nReport: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6a_opus_round2.md`. Page renders are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r2_6a_*`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>145956</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>284421</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
