{"parentUuid":"9a5ac05c-16ca-4528-b678-a16428fd432e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffoNMC9jqCdXSC5ye2mt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014tVM7XExC8TCHj45AaRbvY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 6c entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6c_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 9 FIX entries, 9 numbered fixes, 3 missing ideas, link suggestions).\n- Standards: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (Windows paths; Mac vault is `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`, baseline `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md`).\n- Log format to copy: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`.\n\nFiles: the 19 entries in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6c.txt`, in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. Another fixer is editing 6b files in the same folder right now, and 6d is in review: edit ONLY 6c files.\n\nSource: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx (0-based) = printed + 11, covered PDF 363-379 (plus 288, 299-301, 305, 515, 536). Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/f6c_pN.png` (dpi=300 for Figs 6.25 and 6.30) and open with Read for anything you touch; read graph values yourself and write \"about\".\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n- Fix 2: confirm on PDF 515 that the Addendum is Verkhoshansky's own paper (translated by Yessis). Then any Addendum (PDF 514-590) statement in a 6c entry is \"Verkhoshansky (Addendum)\", not \"the authors\". Also list in your log, under \"Follow-up for the coordinator\", every OTHER staged or vault Supertraining entry that cites PDF 514-590 with \"the authors\" (grep the staging folder and `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/` for \"PDF p. 5[1-9][0-9]\" and \"536\"). Do not edit them.\n- Links to 6b/6d files (fixes 2 and 4): before adding, confirm the target file exists at that moment (6b is being fixed and might rename); if it does not exist, record it in the log instead of linking.\n- Missing ideas: fold each into an existing 6c entry where it fits; if an existing library entry already covers it (the review names 4.3.3 and Ch1.3 candidates), add a Related link instead; write a new entry only if neither works, then append it to the 6c scope file.\n- No renames unless required; if you rename, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths and report any other file linking the old slug.\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines, baseline quotes carry line number and tag, blank line between sections.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6c_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: grep each fixed file for the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and paste the lines for 6c files and the total. Paste both in your final reply and at