{"parentUuid":"97c3c553-0b87-446b-a66a-0cc2a6b3bcfb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffoPWCQtddaSw2HjkVRE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 6c review is back: GO AFTER FIXES. 10 entries passed, 9 need fixes, and none failed. A fixer is working on 6c now.\n\n**What needs fixing in 6c**\n- **Chart values:** a few values were read wrong from two charts.\n- **Labels and links:** some page references, \"Inference:\" labels and links are missing or wrong.\n- **One contradiction is in the wrong place.** One entry says the book contradicts itself about the order of exercises inside one session. The page it points to is about the order of training stages, not sessions. The real rule for the order inside a session is on another page.\n\n**A wider finding: who wrote the Addendum**\n- The Addendum at the end of the book is Verkhoshansky's own paper, translated by Yessis.\n- So it should be credited to \"Verkhoshansky\", not to \"the authors\".\n- Some entries already in the vault may quote the Addendum as \"the authors\". I asked the fixer to list every one of them. It will not change them. I will show you the list.\n\n| Part | Entries | Stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 28 | Ready to promote |\n| 6b | 16 | Fixes running |\n| 6c | 19 | Fixes running |\n| 6d | 25 | First review running |\n\nYou do not need to do anything now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2327,"cache_read_input_tokens":365973,"output_tokens":423,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":365973,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2327,"cache_creation