{"parentUuid":"4778ee98-1556-44e2-97c3-0cf990d10995","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffoaNimFevaxT3tg8XsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014SRQ63Mf9nesCTFNCxjEfW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 6d entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6d_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 11 FIX entries, plus 5 missing ideas and link suggestions).\n- Standards: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (Windows paths; Mac vault is `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`, baseline `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md`).\n- Vault Issurin 2016 brief: find it in `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/research-papers/` (grep \"issurin-2016\"). Read it in full: several fixes depend on exactly what it says (p. 11 favours concentrated models in jumping-type sports; it agrees complex training falls short for elite athletes; it finds no evidence amateurs can't handle concentrated loads; its 28 studies are Issurin's own non-systematic selection).\n- Log format to copy: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`.\n\nFiles: the 25 entries in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch6d.txt`, in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. Other fixers are editing 6b and 6c files in the same folder right now: edit ONLY 6d files.\n\nSource: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx (0-based) = printed + 11, covered PDF 379-403 (plus 305). Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/f6d_pN.png` and open with Read for anything you touch. For Fig 6.39 (PDF ~394-395) render at dpi=400 and read the strength, peak and technique curves yourself before changing them; for Fig 6.32b and Fig 6.36(b) do the same. Values off a graph say \"about\"; anything the image cannot settle is marked unclear.\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page (or in the Issurin brief) before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n- Explosive-strength model: this is the entry that matters most for Eric's football work. After your fixes, the Issurin challenge must say exactly what the brief says, scoped to transferring the model to football (a team sport), and must not claim Issurin rejects it for jumping-type sports.\n- Confidence must be consistent across the 4 Issurin-related entries (explosive model, tri-cyclic, two-mesocycles, complex training): each rating needs a stated reason that fits the brief.\n- Any entry citing the Addendum (PDF 514-590) must attribute it to Verkhoshansky, not \"the authors\" (the Addendum is his own paper, PDF 515).\n- Links to 6b/6c files: confirm each target exists at that moment before adding (those batches are being fixed and could rename); otherwise record it in the log.\n- Missing ideas (5, including Table 6.11 javelin norms and the Table 6.12 cm/m unit error): fold into existing 6d entries where they fit; new entry only if needed, appended to the 6d scope file.\n- No renames unless required; if you rename, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths and report any other file linking the old slug.\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines, baseline quotes carry line number and tag.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch6d_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: grep each fixed file for the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and paste the lines for 6d files and the total. Paste both in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), your Fig 6.39 / 6.32b / 6.36(b) readings, the final confidence and reason for each Issurin-related entry, missing-idea placement, grep proof, lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2494,"cache_read_input_tokens":368300,"output_tokens":1965,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2494,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1965,"cache_read_input_tokens":368300,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2494,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2494},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014SRQ63Mf9nesCTFNCxjEfW":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 6d entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV