 paths\n- Vault library (read-only, dedup greps): `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`\n- Staging library: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`\n- Output folder: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`\n- Source PDF (noisy text layer): `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`\n- Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render every page with a figure, table or number to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/7a_pN.png` (`d[N].get_pixmap(dpi=200).save(...)`) and open it with Read. Write \"about\" for values read off a graph. Only claim \"verified against the page image\" if you opened it.\n\n## Hard rules\n- Add NEW entry files only. Do NOT edit any existing entry and do NOT edit `_book.md` (the coordinator owns it). Chapter 6 entries are being fixed right now in the same folder; do not link to any file whose name starts with a Ch6 topic unless it already existed before today's Ch6 work (prefer links to Ch1-5 and vault entries). Dedup against vault and staging: bodybuilding methods, sets/reps schemes, hypertrophy and intensity methods may be covered by Zatsiorsky, Bompa, Supertraining Ch1-5, and research-paper briefs. Add an entry only for a genuinely new angle and link the existing one in Related; where another library source disagrees, record it and say which. List reciprocal-link suggestions in your report.\n- Use the source's own examples, otherwise start the Example with \"Inference:\". No mechanism the authors do not give. `contested` only for a real contradiction (same question, same quantity) or a named library source that disagrees; give both pages. Locators \"PDF p. X / printed p. Y\" on every number, definition and quote. \"The authors\" unless a passage clearly belongs to one author (a passage naming Verkhoshansky in the third person is Siff 