ining\" (7.4.1 Summary of Movements of the Joints, 7.4.2 Examination of Some Joint Actions), 7.5 \"Use of Strength Training Compendium\" and 7.6 \"Training for Hypertrophy?\", PDF idx 414-431 (printed 403-420). Stop at the end of Chapter 7 (Chapter 8 starts at PDF 432). Another atomizer is working at the same time on the lead-in and 7.1 (PDF 404-413); do not atomize its pages.\n\n## Read first, in full\n1. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (every rule is checked by a reviewer; Windows paths in it, use the Mac translations below).\n2. `/Users/kristinarash/.claude/skills/ingest-book/SKILL.md` (schema, frontmatter keys, file kinds).\n3. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md` (Eric's approved baseline; quote lines verbatim with line number AND tag).\n4. `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md` (map; page key PDF idx = printed + 11, 0-based).\n5. Lessons from the Chapter 5 and 6 reviews: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus.md` and `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6d_opus.md`. Common misses: unlabelled writer judgments, \"contested\" set for things that are not real contradictions, misread figure values, baseline quotes without tags, invented examples, process notes in entry bodies (never mention batches or other agents in an entry).\n6. Two existing entries in the output folder as style references.\n\n## Mac paths\n- Vault library (read-only, dedup greps): `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library` (the `rehab-and-return-to-play` domain, e.g. Harries, may overlap PNF and joint-action material).\n- Staging library: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library`\n- Output folder: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`\n- Source PDF (noisy text layer): `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`\n- T