{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:02:11.129Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa6bbad74ebe17310</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019wgUMfYBvuXqn7VYKw2nTA</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/aa6bbad74ebe17310.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 6b round 2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** 13 GO, 3 FIX, 0 NO-GO. All 11 of round 1's FIX items are resolved in the files. Each of the 3 remaining FIX items is one sentence that a round-1 fix introduced, and none changes a confidence rating.\n\nThe fixes still needed:\n1. **Mesocycle entry:** \"the first is a structural unit, the second a planning unit\" has no label. The book (PDF 327) does use \"structural units\" for the training session, but it never calls the mesocycle a \"planning unit\". Move \"Inference:\" in front of that clause.\n2. **Block-durations entry:** the new sentence says 3-4 weeks \"overlaps them only at 4 weeks\". That is false for \"up to 2 months\", which the same paragraph calls a ceiling, and 3-4 weeks lies inside it. The real conflict is 3-4 weeks (PDF 360, the duration the book says was \"determined\") against 4-8 weeks (PDF 305). `contested` still holds on that pair.\n3. **Functional-specialisation entry:** it says \"the page's cross-references are to 2.2.3 and 5.4.3 only\", but PDF 362 also refers to \"the classification scheme of 6.5\", which the entry itself quotes.\n\nThe checks you asked for:\n- **Fig 6.22 graph A:** I read it myself on a 400 dpi crop. The rise shrinks each year (about 180, 115 and 55 px across Years 1-3) and no peak is drawn. The new descriptions in both entries are correct.\n- **Block-durations conflict:** every figure is on the page as the fixer states: 3-4 weeks (PDF 360), 4-8 weeks (PDF 305), \"up to 2 months\" (PDF 381), the 4-12 week stage, the 4-12 week delayed training effect (LDTE, PDF 375, \"approximately equal to the duration of the strength training stage\"), 1-3 week latency and 18-22 weeks. Only the overlap sentence in fix 2 is wrong.\n- **23-25% monthly volume Inference:** correctly placed in 5.3.3 (PDF 305, before the 5.4 heading) and 6.12.2 (PDF 381), and labelled Inference.\n- **Distributed-vs-concentrated entry:** the Issurin 2016 critique is correctly aimed at Verkhoshansky's concentrated-unidirectional model, matching line 51 of the vault brief. The PDF 371 sentence \"both methods are successful in training athletes of medium qualification\" is verbatim on the page image (the text layer misreads \"are\" as \"arc\").\n- **Fixer's disagreements:** the narrower conflict and the PDF 375 link hold up. The Bondarchuk page range is only half right: section 6.2.2's intensity material continues onto PDF 336. That gets a recommended locator change, not a FIX.\n- **Mechanics:** all 16 files have the six headers, no em dashes outside the headers, no wrapped links and no process wording. All 66 wikilinks resolve. All 19 cited baseline lines match.\n\n**GO entries spot-checked against the page images:**\n- `expectancy-motivation`: PDF 353.\n- `load-must-sit-within-the-current-adaptation-reserve-window`: PDF 360, plus its new Bompa wording against the vault file.\n- `restorative-stage-length`: PDF 361 and 360.\n\nThe other two round-1 GO entries, `build-training-theory` and `situational-leadership`, were checked against the text layer only. Every quote matched.\n\nReport: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6b_opus_round2.md`\nPage renders: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r2_6b_*.png`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>167924</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>371002</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
