ing/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx (0-based) = printed + 11, covered PDF 379-403 (plus 305). Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r2_6d_pN.png` (dpi=400 for Figs 6.39, 6.32b, 6.36b) and open with Read.\n\nScope of this round:\n1. The explosive-strength model entry, in full and with the most care (it matters most for Eric's football work): read Fig 6.39 yourself and check every curve, block and phase statement; every Issurin quote verbatim in the brief or Issurin entries; the football-transfer scoping correct; nothing claims more than the brief says (the fixer reports the brief does NOT say \"jumping-type sports\"; confirm).\n2. The other 10 files round 1 marked FIX, in full: each problem gone, each fixer disagreement justified, nothing new wrong. Read Figs 6.32b and 6.36b yourself.\n3. Confidence consistency: the fixer applied a \"domain rule\" (contested when a library source disagrees inside the sport domain the entry claims) to the four Issurin-related entries. Judge whether it is applied consistently, and whether the long-duration endurance entry (`supported`, a round-1 GO) should be `contested` under the same rule because the brief names swimming. Say which, with the brief's page.\n4. Spot check at least 4 of the round-1 GO entries against the pages.\n5. All wikilinks in the 25 files resolve (staging or vault). Every file: six section headers, no em dashes outside headers, no wrapped links, no review-history or process wording.\n\nWrite `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch6d_opus_round2.md`. Final reply: overall verdict (PROMOTE / GO AFTER FIXES with list / NO-GO), GO/FIX/NO-GO counts, which GO entries you spot-checked, and your call on the endurance entry."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{