{"parentUuid":"4ecce831-8e9e-428f-a7cb-45c895460872","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffq1UMePs8pWLsQTbDkY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 6d fixes are done, and its second review is running now.\n\n**What the 6d fixer changed**\n- **All 11 fixes are in.** It disagreed with the reviewer in 7 places, and it wrote down why in each case.\n- **A wrong paraphrase.** Issurin's 2016 paper does not say \"jumping-type sports\". The reviewer and my own instructions both had that wrong. The paper only says the model suits sports that depend on one narrow quality. The entry now quotes the paper's exact words.\n- **The football model:** it is still marked \"contested\". The reason is now:\n  - Issurin's own book disagrees with the model's structure.\n  - Issurin's 2016 paper argues against using the model in team sports such as football.\n- **One rule for all 4 entries.** An entry is marked \"contested\" when another source disagrees inside the sports the entry is about. Under that rule, the tri-cyclic model is now \"contested\" too.\n- **One open question.** Under the same rule, one more entry, about endurance sports, may need \"contested\", because the Issurin paper names swimming. I asked the second reviewer to decide.\n\nThe lint check shows 4 new broken links. They are all in the Chapter 7 drafts, which link to entries the writers have not written yet. Nothing is broken in Chapter 6.\n\n| Part | Entries | Stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 28 | Ready to promote |\n| 6b | 16 | Ready to promote |\n| 6c | 19 | Second review running |\n| 6d | 25 | Second review running |\n| 7a | — | Writing |\n| 7b | — | Writing |\n\nYou do not need to do anything now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2049,"cache_read_input_tokens":403380,"output_tokens":544,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_