{"parentUuid":"f8909486-b51e-4503-ac7e-8d1cc48dc540","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffq4HqTy9oWBzP6UxWCX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0137qMu49WBA5XEBHyCPPBfb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky && sed -n 22p heuristic--within-session-order-of-explosive-means-matters-less-than-volume-and-contrast.md; grep -o \"which reconciles those two readings; the PDF p. [^;.]*[;.]\" principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum.md","description":"Read the contested paragraph and LDTE sentence"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":407719,"output_tokens":284,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":19},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":407719,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0137qMu49WBA5XEBHyCPPBfb":{"command":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky && sed -n 22p heuristic--within-session-order-of-explosive-means-matters-less-than-volume-and-contrast.md; grep -o \"which reconciles those two readings; the PDF p. [^;.]*[;.]\" principle--long-term-delayed-training-effect-from-volume-above-the-optimum.md","description":"Read the contested paragraph and LDTE sentence"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cffq4GkEXqBNkg5cCMSNh","type":"assistant","uuid":"e58b1d8b-6844-424f-a345-fd59ed7e08db","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:08:14.807Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"e58b1d8b-6844-424f-a345-fd59ed7e08db","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ce914f6b-f81b-42fd-a40b-4c5550786125","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0137qMu49WBA5XEBHyCPPBfb","type":"tool_result","content":"**When NOT to apply** — **Contested inside the book.** On PDF p. 371 order is ranked below volume and contrast but still to be kept (\"fairly unimportant,\" then \"Nevertheless, one should still preserve the above order\"): a hedge, not a contradiction. The book contradicts itself across chapters on within-session order. PDF p. 288 / printed p. 277: resistance plus plyometrics works best \"provided the resistance movements precede the plyometric activities in individual sessions\" (checked against the page image). PDF p. 299 / printed p. 288, novices: \"There was no statistically significant difference\" between strength-first and speed-strength-first within the workout (checked against the page image; [[case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments]]). PDF p. 300 / printed p. 289, \"Research with novices and athletes of average qualification\": \"Least effective is the sequence of strength followed by speed-strength means during the same session\" (checked against the page image). Inference: reading barbell work as \"strength\" and jumping as \"speed-strength\" (Fig 5.13 on the same page labels the jumping means \"Jumps\"), this opposes p. 371's \"preserve the above order\" for \"barbell exercises and jumping exercises.\" The PDF p. 301 bullets (\"Strength exercises should be done after speed-strength exercises in training\"; \"Strong-acting plyometric methods should be done after strength exercises, but not before\") are stage-level: they sit under \"The following principles for the sequential use of training means over a given period emerge\" (PDF p. 300), so they belong with [[heuristic--sequential-accumulation-needs-4-6-week-stages-extensive-before-explosive]], not here. Keep this within-session rule separate from the long-term sequence across stages, where the authors say order does matter: extensive submaximal resistance first, then explosive work, and \"The reverse sequence of this loading scheme leads to a negative cumulative effect\" (PDF p. 372). Inference: Issurin's session rules put the dominant or technical task first and add other modalities after it ([[block-periodization--issurin/principle--training-modality-compatibility-in-a-workout]]), a stricter view of order than this passage. The authors say endurance interactions are a different case, where order clearly matters ([[framework--positive-and-negative-sequences-of-endurance-loading]]).\nwhich reconciles those two readings; the PDF p. 305 figure is a separate quantity.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"90d9f025-1c24-4737-878d-822b7b75a7ed","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:08:15.038Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**When NOT to apply** — **Contested inside the book.** On PDF p. 371 order is ranked below volume and contrast but still to be kept (\"fairly unimportant,\" then \"Nevertheless, one should still preserve the above order\"): a hedge, not a contradiction. The book contradicts itself across chapters on within-session order. PDF p. 288 / printed p. 277: resistance plus plyometrics works best \"provided the resistance movements precede the plyometric activities in individual sessions\" (checked against the page image). PDF p. 299 / printed p. 288, novices: \"There was no statistically significant difference\" between strength-first and speed-strength-first within the workout (checked against the page image; [[case-study--novice-strength-and-speed-strength-sequencing-experiments]]). PDF p. 300 / printed p. 289, \"Research with novices and athletes of average qualification\": \"Least effective is the sequence of strength followed by speed-strength means during the same session\" (checked against the page image). Inference: reading barbell work as \"strength\" and jumping as \"speed-strength\" (Fig 5.13 on the same page labels the jumping means \"Jumps\"), this opposes p. 371's \"preserve the above order\" for \"barbell exercises and jumping exercises.\" The PDF p. 301 bullets (\"Strength exercises should be done after speed-strength exercises in training\"; \"Strong-acting plyometric methods should be done after strength exercises, but not before\") are stage-level: they sit under \"The following principles for the sequential use of training means over a given period emerge\" (PDF p. 300), so they belong with [[heuristic--sequential-accumulation-needs-4-6-week-stages-extensive-before-explosive]], not here. Keep this within-session rule separate from the long-term sequence across stages, where the authors say order does matter: extensive submaximal resistance first, then explosive work, and \"The reverse sequence of this loading scheme leads to a negative cumulative effect\" (PDF p. 372). Inference: Issurin's session rules put the dominant or technical task first and add other modalities after it ([[block-periodization--issurin/principle--training-modality-compatibility-in-a-workout]]), a stricter view of order than this passage. The authors say endurance interactions are a different case, where order clearly matters ([[framework--positive-and-negative-sequences-of-endurance-loading]]).\nwhich reconciles those two readings; the PDF p. 305 figure is a separate quantity.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e58b1d8b-6844-424f-a345-fd59ed7e08db","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
