{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:18:36.487Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae3759d4d7a415649</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01GVkcfUEjPoSYjYNw7aE61n</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/ae3759d4d7a415649.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 7b round 1\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** Of the 14 entries, 4 are GO, 10 need fixes and none is NO-GO. Most of the fixes are small.\n\nI opened every page from PDF 414 to 431 as an image, including 414-418, which the writer had read only as text. Figs 7.10 and 7.12 I zoomed. All the \"Eric's baseline:\" quotes match their line numbers and tags, and every wikilink points to a file that exists. Neither the voice handling nor the physics and anatomy statements needs a change:\n- **7.2 is Siff's:** the page backs this, but Siff is only named on PDF 429 / p.418, and the entries cite PDF 430 alone.\n- **Powermetrics passage:** it is correctly marked as an Inference that it's \"probably Siff\".\n- **7.6 commentator quotes:** they are not presented as the authors' own statements.\n- **Starling's law, Wolff's law and the multifidus claim:** each is quoted as the book's words, and every comment on them is labelled Inference.\n- **Table 7.1 and Fig 7.13:** every value matches the page.\n- **60-70% vs 50-70% power-load range:** both figures appear on the cited pages.\n- **\"Some three times greater\":** the gap with the table is real. The table gives about 2.3 to 2.4 times; the plotted figures give about 2.8 to 3.\n\n**Required fixes, one per line:**\n1. **All six 7.2 entries:** add PDF 429 / p.418 to the Siff attribution and use the page's wording, \"the author ... (Siff, 1989)\".\n2. **PNF framework:** add principle 4, \"Exercising of related muscle groups\", which is missing from the grouped list.\n3. **Activation/relaxation:** the 7.5 quote is misread. The book's \"the latter\" means the main exercises, not the stretching. Also, CR and SRHR do come with repetition counts (\"a few\", \"several\"), so \"without dosages\" is wrong.\n4. **Fradd:** Fig 7.10 is on PDF 423 / p.412, not 424. Raise `untested` to `supported`, limited to the measured table. Fig 7.12 does show a faint shoulder at about 30%, so soften \"double peak not visible\". Give the ratio as 2.3 to 2.4.\n5. **Box squat:** Frost 2010 and Rhea 2009 are both in the vault and say what the entry claims. But Frost contradicts the book's transfer and \"used very effectively\" claim, not its item 1, because item 1 compares a heavier total load with plain free weight. Also, the explanation given for item 4 is not in the book, so it needs an \"Inference:\" label.\n6. **Powermetrics:** the Jandacka sample was 55 male and 48 female physical-education students. The vault summary of the paper never says \"untrained\".\n7. **Trunk:** the book contradicts itself and the entry should say so. Its 7.4.1 summary lists only rectus abdominis and psoas for trunk flexion, and only the obliques for rotation. Both disagree with 7.4.2.\n\n**The 7 `untested` ratings:** Fradd is the only one rated too low, since it has measured data. The other six are claims without data (analogy, opinion, illustration or terminology), so `untested` fits them.\n\n**Duplicates:** none found. No existing entry covers core stability or unstable-surface training.\n\nThe report also lists 5 ideas no entry covers. These include apparent mistakes in the book's 7.4.1 joint-action tables (posterior deltoid listed for sagittal-plane shoulder flexion, and an elbow-rotation note) and the point that curls work more than the biceps.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/`:\n- `review_supertraining_ch7b_opus.md`\n- page images: `_renders/r7b_p414.png` to `r7b_p431.png`, plus zoomed `r7b_p423_fig710.png` and `r7b_p424_fig712.png`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>210362</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>37</tool_uses><duration_ms>386215</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
