d` to `supported`, scope it in the entry to the measured table only, and keep the figure-based claims hedged with \"about\".\n- Fix 5 (box squat): check Frost 2010 and Rhea 2009 in `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/research-papers/` yourself and state exactly which book claim each bears on.\n- Fix 7 (trunk): record the 7.4.1 vs 7.4.2 contradiction with both pages; set `contested` only if it is the same question (which muscles produce trunk flexion/rotation).\n- Missing ideas: the joint-action table errors in 7.4.1 are reference-list errors; record them as a source note in an existing 7b entry if one fits (e.g. the trunk entry), labelled as the writer's reading (Inference), rather than writing a new entry. Fold the other ideas into existing 7b entries where they fit; write a new entry only if needed, then append it to the 7b scope file.\n- No renames unless required; if you rename, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths and report any other file linking the old slug.\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines, baseline quotes carry line number and tag.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7b_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: grep each fixed file for the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and paste the lines for 7b files and the total. Paste both in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), confidence changes, missing-idea placement, grep proof, lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","sto