{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:19:54.956Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac92aa16c6a4259d5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01HqRDAVE48EkoMMwkCnW94N</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/ac92aa16c6a4259d5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 7a round 1\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Overall verdict: GO AFTER FIXES.** GO 3, FIX 7, NO-GO 0.\n\n- **GO:** the Figs 7.1 and 7.2 chart, the miscellaneous bodybuilding sets, and the 27 sticking-point strategies.\n- **FIX:** the other seven entries. Two of them (hybrid and segmental) need only one-line label fixes.\n\n**Required fixes:**\n1. **Maximal methods:** narrow the `contested` reason to the one rest figure for singles. Page 406 gives the 1-5 minutes as rest \"between sets\", while page 409's \"a few seconds\" leads straight into cluster training, so the two may be different methods. Also drop the claim that the book gives a risk warning for forced reps; it gives one only for eccentrics and cheating.\n2. **Three bodybuilding regimes:** change the rating to `supported`, and label the split-routine/zone sentence \"Inference:\".\n3. **Set structures:** change the rating to `supported`, and label the step-method purpose and \"not for a peaking block\" as \"Inference:\".\n4. **Interval training and cluster sets:** the conflict is stronger than the entry shows. The same paragraph that sets the 5RM minimum also uses 4-6RM loads and a 10-20% load drop, both below it (pages 409-410). Lead the `contested` reason with that.\n5. **Hybrid:** label the \"time or space is short\" clause as \"Inference:\". The superscript question is settled by the book's own notation (PDF 336 / printed 325): it is the number of sets, so 80³ means three sets.\n6. **Segmental:** the authors give the random variant a preventive use (avoiding early accommodation, PDF 410), not a fix for a stalled block. Restate it, or label it \"Inference:\".\n7. **Contrast methods:** narrow `contested` to the heavy-light set. The Western studies on PDF 175 tested a lighter effort after a loaded one; they did not test releasing the load mid-repetition (load release, pneumatics). The same page also reports Russian studies that found a positive effect. The entry quotes only the negative side, so add the positive findings.\n\n**On your special-attention points:**\n- **Confidence:** the folder rates prescriptions unevenly (Table 1.1 is `supported`, the Ch5 circuit-layout catalogue is `untested`). I applied one rule: established, parameterised practice is `supported`; anecdotes, novelties the authors discount, tip lists and unevidenced orderings are `untested`. Only the regimes and set-structures entries change. If Eric would rather keep catalogues at `untested`, the Table 1.1 entry should come down too.\n- **The three `contested` entries:** each conflict holds but needs narrowing, as in fixes 1, 4 and 7.\n- **Figures:** every category, filing and connector claim for Figs 7.1 and 7.2 matches the image at 300 dpi.\n- **Voice:** there is no Siff first-person passage on PDF 404-414, so \"the authors\" is correct throughout.\n- **Sticking-point list:** it runs 1-28 with no item 19, so 27 items. The entry's groups use each number once and summarise rather than reprint.\n- **Other checks:** all 13 baseline quotes, line numbers and tags match, and every wikilink resolves. There are no duplicates. The report also lists 5 ideas from these pages that no entry captures, led by the superslow method and the authors' advice to build connective tissue first.\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7a_opus.md`, and the page renders I checked are in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/r7a_p*.png`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>199041</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>441759</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
