{"parentUuid":"569163c6-d1c3-45fd-af11-df3a0f6c1b27","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqxBwDAfVrchK4KCbAw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BgG1uGh31vYAAXiTJiEkQL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 7a entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7a_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 7 FIX entries, 7 numbered fixes, 5 missing ideas).\n- Standards: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (Windows paths; Mac vault is `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`, baseline `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md`).\n- Log format to copy: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`.\n\nFiles: the 10 entries in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch7a.txt`, in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. A 7b fixer is editing other files in the same folder right now, and 6d is in review: edit ONLY 7a files.\n\nSource: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf`, PDF idx (0-based) = printed + 11, covered PDF 404-414 (top of 414), plus 175 and 336. Text: `~/.local/bin/uv run --with pymupdf python3 -c \"import pymupdf; d=pymupdf.open('<pdf>'); print(d[N].get_text())\"`. Render to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_renders/f7a_pN.png` and open with Read for anything you touch.\n\nRules:\n- Verify each review claim on the page before applying. If the review is wrong, do not apply it; record why under \"Disagreements with the review\".\n- Confidence rule (coordinator decision, apply it): established, parameterised practice that the authors present with loads, reps, rest or other parameters is `supported`; anecdotes, novelties the authors discount, tip lists and orderings with no evidence are `untested`. Apply this to fixes 2 and 3 as the review recommends, and check the other 7a entries against the same rule; change any other rating only if the rule clearly requires it, and record each in the log.\n- Fix 5 (hybrid): confirm on PDF 336 / printed 325 that the book's superscript notation means number of sets before writing it.\n- Fix 7 (contrast methods): narrow `contested` to the heavy-light set and add the Russian studies' positive findings from PDF 175 with their exact wording.\n- Missing ideas (superslow, connective tissue first, and others): the writer said some are already covered by existing entries (`framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology`, the 1.6.2 connective-tissue material). Link those in Related of the relevant 7a entry instead of writing a new entry; write a new entry only for an idea no existing entry covers, then append it to the 7a scope file.\n- No renames unless required; if you rename, use `mv` with fully literal absolute paths and report any other file linking the old slug (7b links some 7a files).\n- Do not touch `_book.md` or the vault.\n- Brief rules hold: label every voice, locators on every number and quote, no em dashes in titles or body (section headers keep `**What it is** —`), no review history, never wrap a [[wikilink]] across lines, baseline quotes carry line number and tag.\n- Write the log to `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch7a_applied.md` (Fixer: Claude Opus. Date: 2026-10-03).\n- Prove the fixes landed: grep each fixed file for the new wording. Run `cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint && ~/.local/bin/uv run python3 staging/_tmp/lint_mac.py staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky` and paste the lines for 7a files and the total. Paste both in your final reply and at the end of the log.\n- No git. No vault edits.\n\nFinal reply: per-fix outcome (applied / disagreed), every confidence change with reason, missing-idea placement, grep proof, lint output."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2231,"cache_read_input_tokens":427411,"output_tokens":1823,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":89},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2231,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1823,"cache_read_input_tokens":427411,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2231},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BgG1uGh31vYAAXiTJiEkQL":{"description":"Fix Supertraining 7a entries","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are the fixer in Flint's ingest review gate. Apply the fixes from a round-1 review to staged library entries, check each against the source yourself, and write a fix log.\n\nRead first:\n- Review: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7a_opus.md` (GO AFTER FIXES: 7 FIX entries, 7 numbered fixes, 5 missing ideas).\n- Standards: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md` (Windows paths; Mac vault is `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library`, baseline `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/method-baseline.md`).\n- Log format to copy: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/fixes_supertraining_ch5b_applied.md`.\n\nFiles: the 10 entries in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch7a.txt`, in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/stagi