{"parentUuid":"ed4b156c-2d0c-4c00-b14c-4483539e50c5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqyHP9vghEKbY9Kirer","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 7a review is back: GO AFTER FIXES. 3 entries passed, 7 need fixes, and none failed. A fixer is working on 7a now.\n\n**The 7a fixes**\n- The 3 \"contested\" entries were each too broad. Each one now names only the real conflict. For example, the heavy-then-light set method is contested, but releasing the load in the middle of a rep is a different method, so it is not.\n- One entry quoted only the studies that found no effect. It now also gives the Russian studies that found a positive effect.\n- Some lines need an \"Inference:\" label.\n\n**My decision on ratings**\n- **The question:** should a method the book describes, but gives no proof for, be rated \"untested\" or \"supported\"?\n- **My rule:** if the book gives the method with clear numbers (loads, reps, rest), it is \"supported\". Tips, anecdotes, and things the book itself doubts stay \"untested\".\n- **What it changes:** 2 entries in 7a move up to \"supported\".\n- **If you prefer stricter ratings:** say so, and I will switch them back. One older entry would then come down too.\n\n| Part | Entries | Stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a, 6b, 6c | 63 | Ready to promote |\n| 6d | 25 | Second review running |\n| 7a | 10 | Fixes running |\n| 7b | 14 | Fixes running |\n\nYou do not need to do anything now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":429642,"output_tokens":462,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2249,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":462,"cache_read_input_tokens":429642,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2249},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffqyGhUZtGTU8EKCv72x","type":"assistant","uuid":"937de0f5-9931-4f7d-9d8e-ef13806217c6","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:20:15.399Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
