d":"cd /Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky && grep -n \"^confidence\\|same Issurin 2016 challenge\" framework--annual-models-for-medium-and-long-duration-endurance-sports.md; grep -o \"[^.]*same Issurin 2016 challenge[^.]*\\.\" framework--annual-models-for-medium-and-long-duration-endurance-sports.md; grep -rn \"visible benefits for the preparation of low- and mid-level\" ~/SecondBrain/Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/block-periodization--issurin/ | cut -c1-260; grep -n \"amateur\\|beginners\" claim--complex-training-falls-short-for-highly-qualified-athletes.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n -o \"A terminology tension inside the book[^.]*\\.\" claim--two-large-mesocycles-a-year-bi-cyclic-organisation.md","description":"Locate 6d fix targets and Issurin 2008 quote"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cffr6LTQRMp3rV7S1DLnX","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfc13e9b-a2b0-468f-9f53-5c968888c5f4","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:21:51.348Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"dfc13e9b-a2b0-468f-9f53-5c968888c5f4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"189515d2-55e8-482a-8b52-f518760b72bc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016zPDbburPSZ4FADfz76R4i","type":"tool_result","content":"9:confidence: supported\n35:**When NOT to apply** — Long-duration sports are given a monocycle, while the 6.13 aims call for \"at least two large mesocycles... even in sports which traditionally... use monocyclic periodisation\" (PDF p. 389); the monocycle here still provides \"a two-stage organisation of strength and speed training\" (PDF p. 396), and [[claim--two-large-mesocycles-a-year-bi-cyclic-organisation]] reads the two passages as a terminology tension (number of mesocycles versus number of competition peaks), not opposed positions. The models are for qualified athletes and carry the same Issurin 2016 challenge to concentrated loading as the other 6.14 models ([[framework--bi-cyclic-annual-model-for-explosive-strength-sports]]). Fig 6.46's caption says \"A is the block of concentrated strength loading,\" but the figure prints \"GPP\" under A and \"Strength Load\" under B; which wave is the strength block is unclear.\n The models are for qualified athletes and carry the same Issurin 2016 challenge to concentrated loading as the other 6.\n19:- **The supporting research is old and used weak athletes.** The early studies (Krestovnikov, 1951; Letunov et al., 1954; Zimkin, 1956; Korobkov et al, 1960) found complex loading gave balanced fitness and better strength, speed and endurance than unidirectional work. Separately, \"Parallel loading of different emphasis was shown to simultaneously improve different physiological functions in the\n29:**When NOT to apply** — **Contested by Issurin on the remedy and on the beginners limit, not on the critique (the basis for the `contested` rating).** Issurin agrees that traditional complex training falls short for elite athletes: the library's brief of Issurin 2016 says the review \"repeats the book's critique of traditional planning,\" where \"the book\" is Issurin's own Block Periodization ([[r\n22:A terminology tension inside the book, not two opposed positions.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a81da6fd-235e-4655-bb23-3c8d6a1b863c","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:21:51.630Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9:confidence: supported\n35:**When NOT to apply** — Long-duration sports are given a monocycle, while the 6.13 aims call for \"at least two large mesocycles... even in sports which traditionally... use monocyclic periodisation\" (PDF p. 389); the monocycle here still provides \"a two-stage organisation of strength and speed training\" (PDF p. 396), and [[claim--two-large-mesocycles-a-year-bi-cyclic-organisation]] reads the two passages as a terminology tension (number of mesocycles versus number of competition peaks), not opposed positions. The models are for qualified athletes and carry the same Issurin 2016 challenge to concentrated loading as the other 6.14 models ([[framework--bi-cyclic-annual-model-for-explosive-strength-sports]]). Fig 6.46's caption says \"A is the block of concentrated strength loading,\" but the figure prints \"GPP\" under A and \"Strength Load\" under B; which wave is the strength block is unclear.\n The models are for qualified athletes and carry the same Issurin 2016 challenge to concentrated loading as the other 6.\n19:- **The supporting research is old and used weak athletes.** The early studies (Krestovnikov, 1951; Letunov et al., 1954; Zimkin, 1956; Korobkov et al, 1960) found complex loading gave balanced fitness and better strength, speed and endurance than unidirectional work. Separately, \"Parallel loading of different emphasis was shown to simultaneously improve different physiological functions in the\n29:**When NOT to apply** — **Contested by Issurin on the remedy and on the beginners limit, not on the critique (the basis for the `contested` rating).** Issurin agrees that traditional complex training falls short for elite athletes: the library's brief of Issurin 2016 says the review \"repeats the book's critique of traditional planning,\" where \"the book\" is Issurin's own Block Periodization ([[r\n22:A terminology tension inside the book, not two opposed positions.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dfc13e9b-a2b0-468f-9f53-5c968888c5f4","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
