{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:32:49.689Z","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9a1c8b9128c8b70d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01GKxRJTWLkF3yZke3vUrYz1</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c/tasks/a9a1c8b9128c8b70d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review Supertraining 7b round 2\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Verdict: GO AFTER FIXES. GO 10, FIX 4, NO-GO 0.**\n\nThe report is at `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/review_supertraining_ch7b_opus_round2.md`.\n\nAll seven round-1 fix groups landed and match the pages. I checked them in the files themselves, not in the fix log.\n- **Siff attribution:** all six 7.2 entries now cite PDF 429 and 430 with the page's own wording. Principle 4 is in the list.\n- **Activation entry:** \"the latter\" is fixed. The fixer was right that the book gives both \"several times\" and \"a few repetitions\" for contract-relax (PDF 417).\n- **Fradd:** the dual locator is right (figure on PDF 423, quote on PDF 424). I checked the table values, ratios and figure readings at 300 dpi.\n- **Frost, Rhea and Jandacka:** every statement matches the vault briefs.\n- **Trunk entry staying `supported`:** I agree. The 7.4.1 summary never says \"only\" or \"solely\". 7.4.2 adds muscles to it and reverses nothing, so the rule for `contested` is not met.\n\nThe four FIX entries each need a one-sentence change:\n1. **Fradd:** When to apply opens with \"free weight for peak power, combined resistance for high force across the range\", unlabelled. The book makes no such rule, and it lets `supported` reach past the Table 7.1 comparison. It needs an \"Inference:\" label.\n2. **Box squat:**\n   - The Rhea Inference says the study \"does not separate the bands from the fast bar speed\". It does: it had a fast-only group, and the bands' added effect was not significant (p = .09).\n   - Two sentences judging what Frost does and does not contradict need an \"Inference:\" label.\n3. **Powermetrics:** the new Inference applies \"even more forceful than drop-and-catch\" to all four forms. PDF 426 says it of the two active forms only, and says \"can be\".\n4. **Trunk:** the new note on the book's elbow error is itself imprecise. Forearm rotation happens at two radioulnar joints. One is at the wrist, so the book's \"at the wrist\" is half right. The other is inside the elbow joint capsule, which is the real problem with the book's \"no rotation of the elbow joint as a whole\".\n\nThe four GO entries I spot-checked against the pages all hold. Across the 14 files:\n- every file has the six section headers;\n- there are no em dashes outside the headers and no wrapped links;\n- all 49 wikilinks resolve;\n- there is no review-history wording.\n\nOnce the four changes are made, a grep for the new wording is enough; there is no need for a third review round.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>175648</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>237994</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
