xactly once in its file.\n1. **Training-effect taxonomy (`framework--acute-delayed-particular-cumulative-training-effect-taxonomy`), 2 edits.** The book's \"(see 6.7.1)\" points at a section that doesn't exist, because 6.7 has no subsections. The fix points to the 6.9.1 training-effect entry and keeps the note that no rest-interval rule is given.\n2. **Shock methods, 2 edits.** The \"7.1 (not yet ingested)\" notes become links to the two 7.1 entries that define these methods.\n3. **Non-commutative training order, 1 edit.** The 7.1 placeholder becomes a link to the hybrid-training entry.\n4. **Physical-quality transfer, 1 edit.** It now links the 6.12.2 complex-training claim. \"Later chapters\" stays because Chapter 8 isn't in yet. This reverses the decision the Chapter 5 table made to leave this line alone.\n5. **Two Evans entries, 1 edit each.** Their Related paragraph ends on a stray `&lt;/content&gt;` line, so the script would have appended the link onto that line.\n\n**Dropped: 9 items**, each with its reason in the file.\n- 2 in-batch suggestions are already linked.\n- 1 suggestion would add a link from a new entry to an old one, which isn't a reciprocal link.\n- 1 in-batch pair was never flagged by anyone.\n- The Evans pairs went to Manual edits instead.\n- 1 alternative target was not used.\n- 3 pointers are left as they are because no section is named or no Chapter 6–7 entry fits.\n\n**Doubts**\n- **Three fixer-only in-batch rows.** The brief allowed in-batch rows only where a reviewer flagged the pair. Three rows were flagged by a fixer alone: the long-term delayed-effect principle to the Antonova/Levchenko case, the technique-timing heuristic to the loading-reduction heuristic, and the loading-volume principle to the method chart. They're marked \"Fixer only\" in the Origin column. Cut them if you want the rule applied strictly.\n- **377 unreciprocated links.** None of the 377 links from the 112 new entries into older entries has a back-link yet. That is out of scope here, but it could be a later wave.\n- **Chapter 5 table already applied.** Its links are already in the vault, and the row notes assume that.\n- **Stale sentence in an old entry.** `framework--functional-vs-structural-resistance-training` says balance-board training is \"a different, later usage the text does not address\". Section 7.4 now addresses it. I noted this under Dropped but didn't edit it; rewording it is your call.\n- **Stray `&lt;/content&gt;` lines.** I left them in the two Evans files; removing them is a separate cleanup.\n- **Staging copies will fall behind.** 25 of the 27 script-row source files have byte-identical copies under `staging/library/`, and so do all six manual-edit files. Refresh them from the vault before any later promotion, or the new links will be overwritten.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>251005</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>791352</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
