/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/claim--complex-training-falls-short-for-highly-qualified-athletes.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":4,"newStart":30,"newLines":4,"lines":[" "," **Example** — The authors' own example of a complex unit: a workout of \"resistance training, plyometrics and sprinting,\" or a week using those means on different days (PDF p. 379). Their single-emphasis examples are the swimmer and jumper microcycles of Kudelin (1980) and Mironenko (1981) (PDF p. 381)."," ","-**Related** — [[framework--conjugate-sequence-system-of-training-means]], [[framework--sequential-and-concurrent-variants-of-systematic-means]], [[claim--concentrated-strength-loading-limited-period-qualified-athletes-and-volume-saving]], [[case-study--unidirectional-weekly-microcycles-swimming-and-speed-strength]], [[claim--strength-and-speed-training-response-shifts-with-training-age]], [[block-periodization--issurin/principle--concentration-of-training-workloads]], [[research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a]]","+**Related** — [[framework--conjugate-sequence-system-of-training-means]], [[framework--sequential-and-concurrent-variants-of-systematic-means]], [[claim--concentrated-strength-loading-limited-period-qualified-athletes-and-volume-saving]], [[case-study--unidirectional-weekly-microcycles-swimming-and-speed-strength]], [[claim--strength-and-speed-training-response-shifts-with-training-age]], [[block-periodization--issurin/principle--concentration-of-training-workloads]], [[research-papers/issurin-2016-benefits-and-limitations-of-block-periodized-training-approaches-to-athletes-preparation-a]]; [[claim--concentrated-beats-distributed-loading-for-highly-qualified-athletes]] (6.9.5, distributed and concentrated loading both work at medium qualification while highly qualified athletes need concentration; the same qualification split; rated contested)"]}]}],"mor