{"parentUuid":"bd863f79-c76d-4a09-84c8-465904db2727","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffvhfru8fjr2PJemQSKr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The error log is empty, and today's transcript was updated 18 minutes ago. Writing the handoff now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":495742,"output_tokens":2355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":75},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2355,"cache_read_input_tokens":495742,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cffvhex5YMhRanyimrGSr","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea798aee-ebae-473f-a218-0c1729c6ce8a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:22:15.088Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
{"parentUuid":"ea798aee-ebae-473f-a218-0c1729c6ce8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffvhfru8fjr2PJemQSKr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013T9ZdXhsz96wF8ChbF6osU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/handoffs/2026-10-03-supertraining-ch4-7-mac.md","content":"# Handoff 2026-10-03 (Mac): *Supertraining* Chapters 4.3 to 7 promoted\n\n## What was worked on and why\n\nEric picked up Flint on the Mac (Saturday). The Jev pass needs the Windows-only catalog, so the session ran the next queue item that works on the Mac: the *Supertraining* ingest (Siff and Verkhoshansky, 6th Expanded). It moved from Chapter 4.3 to the end of Chapter 7 in one day, every batch through the two-stage review gate, and promoted all of it on Eric's approval.\n\n## Result\n\n| Batch | Sections | Entries | SecondBrain commits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ch4.3-4.4 | Dynamic correspondence, strength and endurance | 23 | `8d0909e`, links `104eb0e` |\n| Ch5 (5a, 5b, 5c) | Methods of special strength training | 75 | `3109157`, Bompa fix `75f846d`, links `51ee50f` |\n| Ch6 (6a-6d) | Organisation of training | 88 | `2708d36`, links `e0170a8` |\n| Ch7 (7a, 7b) | Strength training methods | 24 | `2708d36` (same commit), Addendum fix `d41a087` |\n\n210 new vault entries in `Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. memsearch re-indexed after Ch4 and Ch5; the Ch6-7 re-index was started at the end of the session.\n\n## How the gate ran (Mac, Codex not used)\n\n1. Opus atomizer per batch, chapters split into 2-4 parallel batches with no shared pages; atomizers add files only and never edit `_book.md` (the coordinator owns it).\n2. Fresh Opus round-1 reviewer (falsify, open page images).\n3. Opus fixer (verifies each review claim on the page, logs disagreements).\n4. Fresh Opus round-2 reviewer. Its last one-sentence fixes were applied by the coordinator after checking the page text.\n5. Eric approved each promotion. Then reciprocal-links table (agent-built, dry-run verified), manual edits, sync back, memsearch.\n\nRecords: `staging/review_supertraining_*_opus*.md`, `staging/fixes_supertraining_*_applied.md`, `staging/_scope_supertraining_*.txt`, `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03*.md`.\n\n## Decisions (with the reasoning)\n\n- **Bompa entry fixed (Eric):** `periodization--bompa/principle--concentrated-loading-overreaching` credited \"gains 4 to 12 weeks after the block\" to Siff and Verkhoshansky. That is Bompa & Haff 5e's citation (printed p. 49, PDF idx 60 of `~/DEV/BookInbox/Periodization - Theory and Methodology of Training - 5th.pdf`). *Supertraining* gives a 1-3 week latency (PDF 305) and 4-12 weeks as how long the delayed effect lasts (PDF 375).\n- **Addendum voice (Eric):** 9.1-9.2 (PDF 514-590) is Verkhoshansky's own paper translated by Yessis (PDF 515). Attribute it to him, not \"the authors\".\n- **Domain rule for `contested`:** set it when a library source disagrees inside the sport domain the entry claims. Issurin 2016 does not say \"jumping-type sports\"; it counts against transferring Verkhoshansky's concentrated model to team sports (football) and swimming.\n- **Confidence rule (coordinator, from 7a):** practice the authors give with loads, reps or rest is `supported`; tips, anecdotes, discounted novelties and unevidenced orderings are `untested`. Eric may override.\n\n## Files created or modified\n\n- Flint repo: `staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/` (210 new entries, `_book.md`), plus synced-back copies in `elite-sports-performance--evans/`, `block-periodization--issurin/`, `science-and-practice-of-strength-training--zatsiorsky/`, `transfer-of-training-in-sports--bondarchuk/`; review, fix, scope and link files in `staging/`; `docs/STATUS.md`; this handoff.\n- Local only (gitignored): `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (md5 `d3453c5e...`), `staging/_renders/`, `staging/_tmp/` (Mac-path copies of the four scripts, the Ch7-excluding promote copy, edit scripts, memsearch logs).\n- SecondBrain: the commits listed above.\n\n## Next actions\n\n1. Chapter 8, Designing Sport Specific Strength Programmes, printed 421-480 / PDF idx 432-491 (60 pages). Same gate. The PDF is already staged on the Mac.\n2. Then Chapter 9 Addendum (Verkhoshansky's own, PDF 514-590; attribute to him).\n3. Fix the four Flint scripts to read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json` (they hard-code Windows; the Mac used copies in `staging/_tmp/`).\n4. Later wave: 377 links from the 112 Ch6-7 entries into older entries have no back-link.\n5. Windows still owns the Jev pass (commands in STATUS).\n\n## Mid-flight and open\n\n- memsearch re-index for Ch6-7 was running at closeout; check `staging/_tmp/memsearch-index-2026-10-03-ch6-7.log` (Mac).\n- Eric to delete merged branches (the guard blocks agents): `git branch -d supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6` and `git push origin --delete supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6`.\n- Zotero MCP on the Mac fails with \"MCP tenant gate is not configured\".\n- Small cleanups: two Evans entries end with a stray `</content>` line; `framework--functional-vs-structural-resistance-training` says balance-board training is not addressed, but 7.4 now addresses it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":495742,"output_tokens":2355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":75},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2355,"cache_read_input_tokens":495742,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013T9ZdXhsz96wF8ChbF6osU":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/docs/handoffs/2026-10-03-supertraining-ch4-7-mac.md","content":"# Handoff 2026-10-03 (Mac): *Supertraining* Chapters 4.3 to 7 promoted\n\n## What was worked on and why\n\nEric picked up Flint on the Mac (Saturday). The Jev pass needs the Windows-only catalog, so the session ran the next queue item that works on the Mac: the *Supertraining* ingest (Siff and Verkhoshansky, 6th Expanded). It moved from Chapter 4.3 to the end of Chapter 7 in one day, every batch through the two-stage review gate, and promoted all of it on Eric's approval.\n\n## Result\n\n| Batch | Sections | Entries | SecondBrain commits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ch4.3-4.4 | Dynamic correspondence, strength and endurance | 23 | `8d0909e`, links `104eb0e` |\n| Ch5 (5a, 5b, 5c) | Methods of special strength training | 75 | `3109157`, Bompa fix `75f846d`, links `51ee50f` |\n| Ch6 (6a-6d) | Organisation of training | 88 | `2708d36`, links `e0170a8` |\n| Ch7 (7a, 7b) | Strength training methods | 24 | `2708d36` (same commit), Addendum fix `d41a087` |\n\n210 new vault entries in `Knowledge/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`. memsearch re-indexed after Ch4 and Ch5; the Ch6-7 re-index was started at the end of the session.\n\n## How the gate ran (Mac, Codex not used)\n\n1. Opus atomizer per batch, chapters split into 2-4 parallel batches with no shared pages; atomizers add files only and never edit `_book.md` (the coordinator owns it).\n2. Fresh Opus round-1 reviewer (falsify, open page images).\n3. Opus fixer (verifies each review claim on the page, logs disagreements).\n4. Fresh Opus round-2 reviewer. Its last one-sentence fixes were applied by the coordinator after checking the page text.\n5. Eric approved each promotion. Then reciprocal-links table (agent-built, dry-run verified), manual edits, sync back, memsearch.\n\nRecords: `staging/review_supertraining_*_opus*.md`, `staging/fixes_supertraining_*_applied.md`, `staging/_scope_supertraining_*.txt`, `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-10-03*.md`.\n\n## Decisions (with the reasoning)\n\n- **Bompa entry fixed (Eric):** `periodization--bompa/principle--concentrated-loading-overreaching` credited \"gains 4 to 12 weeks after the block\" to Siff and Verkhoshansky. That is Bompa & Haff 5e's citation (printed p. 49, PDF idx 60 of `~/DEV/BookInbox/Periodization - Theory and Methodology of Training - 5th.pdf`). *Supertraining* gives a 1-3 week latency (PDF 305) and 4-12 weeks as how long the delayed effect lasts (PDF 375).\n- **Addendum voice (Eric):** 9.1-9.2 (PDF 514-590) is Verkhoshansky's own paper translated by Yessis (PDF 515). Attribute it to him, not \"the authors\".\n- **Domain rule for `contested`:** set it when a library source disagrees inside the sport domain the entry claims. Issurin 2016 does not say \"jumping-type sports\"; it counts against transferring Verkhoshansky's concentrated model to team sports (football) and swimming.\n- **Confidence rule (coordinator, from 7a):** practice the authors give with loads, reps or rest is `supported`; tips, anecdotes, discounted novelties and unevidenced orderings are `untested`. Eric may override.\n\n## Files created or modified\n\n- Flint repo: `staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/` (210 new entries, `_book.md`), plus synced-back copies in `elite-sports-performance--evans/`, `block-periodization--issurin/`, `science-and-practice-of-strength-training--zatsiorsky/`, `transfer-of-training-in-sports--bondarchuk/`; review, fix, scope and link files in `staging/`; `docs/STATUS.md`; this handoff.\n- Local only (gitignored): `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (md5 `d3453c5e...`), `staging/_renders/`, `staging/_tmp/` (Mac-path copies of the four scripts, the Ch7-excluding promote copy, edit scripts, memsearch logs).\n- SecondBrain: the commits listed above.\n\n## Next actions\n\n1. Chapter 8, Designing Sport Specific Strength Programmes, printed 421-480 / PDF idx 432-491 (60 pages). Same gate. The PDF is already staged on the Mac.\n2. Then Chapter 9 Addendum (Verkhoshansky's own, PDF 514-590; attribute to him).\n3. Fix the four Flint scripts to read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json` (they hard-code Windows; the Mac used copies in `staging/_tmp/`).\n4. Later wave: 377 links from the 112 Ch6-7 entries into older entries have no back-link.\n5. Windows still owns the Jev pass (commands in STATUS).\n\n## Mid-flight and open\n\n- memsearch re-index for Ch6-7 was running at closeout; check `staging/_tmp/memsearch-index-2026-10-03-ch6-7.log` (Mac).\n- Eric to delete merged branches (the guard blocks agents): `git branch -d supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6` and `git push origin --delete supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6`.\n- Zotero MCP on the Mac fails with \"MCP tenant gate is not configured\".\n- Small cleanups: two Evans entries end with a stray `</content>` line; `framework--functional-vs-structural-resistance-training` says balance-board training is not addressed, but 7.4 now addresses it.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cffvhex5YMhRanyimrGSr","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce2f032c-bd99-49b3-ac13-1e831e58b2ec","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:22:33.299Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","version":"2.1.288","gitBranch":"supertraining-ch4-3-4"}
