f-strength-training--zatsiorsky/`, `transfer-of-training-in-sports--bondarchuk/`; review, fix, scope and link files in `staging/`; `docs/STATUS.md`; this handoff.\n- Local only (gitignored): `staging/books/supertraining-6th-expanded.pdf` (md5 `d3453c5e...`), `staging/_renders/`, `staging/_tmp/` (Mac-path copies of the four scripts, the Ch7-excluding promote copy, edit scripts, memsearch logs).\n- SecondBrain: the commits listed above.\n\n## Next actions\n\n1. Chapter 8, Designing Sport Specific Strength Programmes, printed 421-480 / PDF idx 432-491 (60 pages). Same gate. The PDF is already staged on the Mac.\n2. Then Chapter 9 Addendum (Verkhoshansky's own, PDF 514-590; attribute to him).\n3. Fix the four Flint scripts to read the vault path from `~/.claude/skills/_shared/config.<platform>.json` (they hard-code Windows; the Mac used copies in `staging/_tmp/`).\n4. Later wave: 377 links from the 112 Ch6-7 entries into older entries have no back-link.\n5. Windows still owns the Jev pass (commands in STATUS).\n\n## Mid-flight and open\n\n- memsearch re-index for Ch6-7 was running at closeout; check `staging/_tmp/memsearch-index-2026-10-03-ch6-7.log` (Mac).\n- Eric to delete merged branches (the guard blocks agents): `git branch -d supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6` and `git push origin --delete supertraining-ch4-3-4 supertraining-ch5 supertraining-ch6`.\n- Zotero MCP on the Mac fails with \"MCP tenant gate is not configured\".\n- Small cleanups: two Evans entries end with a stray `</content>` line; `framework--functional-vs-structural-resistance-training` says balance-board training is not addressed, but 7.4 now addresses it.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce2f032c-bd99-49b3-ac13-1e831e58b2ec","session_id":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec6873c","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint","sessionId":"9d08ef48-9f28-44dc-845b-1ca05ec